  field detectorScore type number required true nullable false default 0 semantic "Local detector confidence in [0,1]." mutable false system true readers compare writers index
  field detectorName type string required true nullable false default null semantic "Exact bundled detector identity." mutable false system true readers index,compare writers index
  field modelName type string required true nullable false default null semantic "Exact DINOv2 checkpoint used for the crop." mutable false system true readers index,compare writers index
  field pipelineVersion type string required true nullable false default null semantic "Exact detector, crop, and embedding pipeline version." mutable false system true readers index,compare writers index
  field indexedAt type datetime required true nullable false default null semantic "Successful local subject extraction time." mutable true system true readers compare writers index
  invariant GeneralSubjectObservation.valid_embedding statement "Every retained subject has a finite non-zero normalized vector whose stored dimension matches the model output." refs GeneralSubjectObservation.embedding,GeneralSubjectObservation.dimension
  invariant GeneralSubjectObservation.explicit_bounds statement "Every subject has valid normalized non-empty bounds, a confidence in [0,1], and a stable index." refs GeneralSubjectObservation.boundingBox,GeneralSubjectObservation.detectorScore,GeneralSubjectObservation.subjectIndex
  forbid GeneralSubjectObservation.no_person_or_pet_duplication statement "Person, cat, and dog detections are not persisted here because existing face and pet observations are reused for subject similarity." refs GeneralSubjectObservation.category
  forbid GeneralSubjectObservation.no_crop_retention statement "The padded subject bitmap exists only in memory and is never persisted or transmitted." refs GeneralSubjectObservation.embedding,GeneralSubjectObservation.boundingBox

field SimilarPhotoResultFieldPromise for SimilarPhotoResult:
  label "相似照片结果字段 Promise"
  summary "Represents one derived accessible candidate while keeping independent relationship evidence visible."
  field queryPhotoId type PhotoID required true nullable false default null semantic "Photo for which similarity was requested." mutable false system true readers compare writers -
  field candidatePhotoId type PhotoID required true nullable false default null semantic "Different accessible candidate photo." mutable false system true readers compare writers -
  field relationship type string required true nullable false default visually_similar semantic "Primary display class: burst, same_scene, composition_similar, subject_similar, or visually_similar." mutable false system true readers compare writers -
  field globalSimilarity type number required true nullable false default 0 semantic "Cosine similarity of normalized whole-photo DINOv2 vectors." mutable false system true readers compare writers -
  field compositionSimilarity type number required true nullable false default 0 semantic "Position-preserving aggregate similarity across the sixteen corresponding 4x4 cells." mutable false system true readers compare writers -
  field subjectSimilarity type number required false nullable true default null semantic "Best compatible evidence from registered faces, pets, or general detected subjects; null when none exists." mutable false system true readers compare writers -
  field captureDeltaMillis type integer required false nullable true default null semantic "Absolute capture-time difference when both photos have capture timestamps." mutable false system true readers compare writers -
  field rankScore type number required true nullable false default 0 semantic "Deterministic weighted score derived only from visual, spatial, subject, and time evidence." mutable false system true readers compare writers -
  field explanation type text required true nullable false default "" semantic "Human-readable explanation composed after ranking from relationship evidence and overlapping VLM-derived tags." mutable false system true readers compare writers -
  invariant SimilarPhotoResult.score_bounds statement "All present similarity and rank scores are finite and bounded to [0,1]." refs SimilarPhotoResult.globalSimilarity,SimilarPhotoResult.compositionSimilarity,SimilarPhotoResult.subjectSimilarity,SimilarPhotoResult.rankScore
  invariant SimilarPhotoResult.different_photos statement "A result never compares a photo to the same content identity." refs SimilarPhotoResult.queryPhotoId,SimilarPhotoResult.candidatePhotoId
  invariant SimilarPhotoResult.explanation_after_rank statement "The explanation may quote overlapping local annotation facets or tags only after rank and relationship are fixed." refs SimilarPhotoResult.rankScore,SimilarPhotoResult.explanation
  forbid SimilarPhotoResult.no_vlm_score statement "VLM captions, tags, facets, model confidence, and generated explanations cannot change numeric similarity, relationship classification, or ordering." refs SimilarPhotoResult.relationship,SimilarPhotoResult.rankScore,SimilarPhotoResult.explanation
  forbid SimilarPhotoResult.no_delete_claim statement "Similarity results never imply that either original is duplicate, safe to delete, owned, or mutable." refs SimilarPhotoResult.queryPhotoId,SimilarPhotoResult.candidatePhotoId

field AndroidSearchStateFieldPromise for AndroidSearchState:
  label "Android 搜索状态字段 Promise"
  summary "Derives whether search is usable and which suggestion chips are justified by current annotations."
  field annotationCount type integer required true nullable false default 0 semantic "Number of distinct photos with a current annotation." mutable true system true readers annotate,search writers annotate
  field enabled type boolean required true nullable false default false semantic "Whether the search input and submission action are enabled." mutable true system true readers search writers annotate
  field suggestions type json required true nullable false default "[]" semantic "Deduplicated suggestions derived only from latest accessible annotations, never static presets." mutable true system true readers search writers annotate
  invariant AndroidSearchState.enabled_after_annotation statement "Search is enabled if and only if annotationCount is greater than zero." refs AndroidSearchState.annotationCount,AndroidSearchState.enabled
  invariant AndroidSearchState.no_default_suggestions statement "suggestions is empty before the first annotation and every non-empty suggestion occurs in current annotation metadata." refs AndroidSearchState.annotationCount,AndroidSearchState.suggestions
  forbid AndroidSearchState.no_static_presets statement "Do not populate suggestions from hard-coded example terms or unannotated photos." refs AndroidSearchState.suggestions

function ScanLibraryFunctionPromise action scan:
  label "扫描照片库 Function Promise"
  summary "Discovers supported photo files and refreshes current path presence."
  depends PhotoAssetFieldPromise,PhotoLocationFieldPromise
  trigger "User selects an absolute local directory and invokes scan."
  precondition ScanLibrary.root_exists statement "The selected root exists and is a readable directory." refs PhotoLocation.rootPath
  reads PhotoLocation.path,PhotoLocation.rootPath,PhotoLocation.present,PhotoLocation.modifiedNanoseconds
  writes PhotoAsset.id,PhotoAsset.mediaType,PhotoAsset.byteSize,PhotoAsset.discoveredAt,PhotoLocation.path,PhotoLocation.photoId,PhotoLocation.rootPath,PhotoLocation.present,PhotoLocation.modifiedNanoseconds,PhotoLocation.lastSeenAt
  ensure ScanLibrary.content_addressed statement "Each discovered file maps to a PhotoAsset identified by its SHA-256 bytes." refs PhotoAsset.id,PhotoLocation.photoId
  ensure ScanLibrary.missing_marked statement "Previously known paths beneath this root that are not observed become present=false without deleting history." refs PhotoLocation.rootPath,PhotoLocation.present
  sideeffect ScanLibrary.catalog_only statement "Only the APM catalog is written; source files are never modified." refs PhotoLocation.path
  idempotency "Scanning an unchanged root preserves content identities and updates only observation metadata."
  forbid ScanLibrary.no_source_write statement "Never write, rename, move, or delete a source photo." refs PhotoLocation.path

function TagPhotoFunctionPromise action annotate:
  label "本地模型标注 Function Promise"
  summary "Sends one present photo to a configured local model and appends validated annotation output."
  depends PhotoAssetFieldPromise,PhotoLocationFieldPromise,PhotoAnnotationFieldPromise
  trigger "User requests annotation of unannotated photos or explicitly requests re-annotation."
  precondition TagPhoto.path_present statement "At least one current readable path exists for the photo." refs PhotoLocation.path,PhotoLocation.present
  precondition TagPhoto.local_default statement "The default provider is the loopback Ollama endpoint." refs PhotoAnnotation.modelProvider
  reads PhotoAsset.id,PhotoLocation.path,PhotoLocation.present,PhotoAnnotation.photoId,PhotoAnnotation.modelName,PhotoAnnotation.promptVersion
  writes PhotoAnnotation.id,PhotoAnnotation.photoId,PhotoAnnotation.caption,PhotoAnnotation.tags,PhotoAnnotation.facets,PhotoAnnotation.visibleText,PhotoAnnotation.modelProvider,PhotoAnnotation.modelName,PhotoAnnotation.promptVersion,PhotoAnnotation.createdAt
  ensure TagPhoto.validated_structured_output statement "Caption, tags, structured facets, and visible text are validated against the annotation schema before insertion." refs PhotoAnnotation.caption,PhotoAnnotation.tags,PhotoAnnotation.facets,PhotoAnnotation.visibleText
  ensure TagPhoto.provenance_recorded statement "The exact provider, model name, and prompt version are stored with every successful result." refs PhotoAnnotation.modelProvider,PhotoAnnotation.modelName,PhotoAnnotation.promptVersion
  reject TagPhoto.model_unavailable statement "No annotation is written when the configured model endpoint is unavailable." refs PhotoAnnotation.modelProvider,PhotoAnnotation.modelName
  reject TagPhoto.invalid_output statement "No annotation is written when output fails schema validation." refs PhotoAnnotation.caption,PhotoAnnotation.tags,PhotoAnnotation.facets,PhotoAnnotation.visibleText
  sideeffect TagPhoto.local_inference statement "The photo is sent to the configured loopback Ollama endpoint by default." refs PhotoLocation.path,PhotoAnnotation.modelProvider
  idempotency "Without force, a photo with the same model and prompt version is skipped; force appends a new immutable annotation."
  forbid TagPhoto.no_implicit_remote statement "Never send photo bytes to a non-loopback endpoint without explicit configuration." refs PhotoLocation.path,PhotoAnnotation.modelProvider

function SearchPhotosFunctionPromise action search:
  label "搜索照片 Function Promise"
  summary "Finds current photo paths using the latest annotation per photo."
  depends PhotoLocationFieldPromise,PhotoAnnotationFieldPromise
  trigger "User provides a non-empty text query."
  precondition SearchPhotos.non_empty_query statement "The normalized search query is not empty." refs PhotoAnnotation.caption,PhotoAnnotation.tags,PhotoAnnotation.facets,PhotoAnnotation.visibleText
  reads PhotoLocation.path,PhotoLocation.photoId,PhotoLocation.present,PhotoAnnotation.photoId,PhotoAnnotation.caption,PhotoAnnotation.tags,PhotoAnnotation.facets,PhotoAnnotation.visibleText,PhotoAnnotation.id
  writes -
  ensure SearchPhotos.latest_annotation statement "Matching uses the latest appended annotation for each photo." refs PhotoAnnotation.id,PhotoAnnotation.photoId
  ensure SearchPhotos.current_paths_only statement "Returned paths have present=true." refs PhotoLocation.path,PhotoLocation.present
  reject SearchPhotos.empty_query statement "An empty or whitespace-only query is rejected." refs PhotoAnnotation.caption,PhotoAnnotation.tags,PhotoAnnotation.facets,PhotoAnnotation.visibleText
  sideeffect SearchPhotos.read_only statement "Search does not change catalog or photo files." refs PhotoLocation.path
  idempotency "The same query against unchanged catalog state returns the same ordered results."
  forbid SearchPhotos.no_absent_paths statement "Never return a path whose latest presence state is false." refs PhotoLocation.path,PhotoLocation.present

function ConfigureAndroidModelFunctionPromise action configure:
  label "配置 Android VLM Function Promise"
  summary "Validates and stores the endpoint, model, and explicit remote photo-transfer decision, with a route to local person and pet identity management."
  depends InferenceConfigurationFieldPromise
  trigger "User navigates from the main app bar to the dedicated model-settings screen and saves settings there."
  precondition ConfigureAndroidModel.valid_url statement "The endpoint is an absolute HTTP or HTTPS URL with a host and the model name is non-empty." refs InferenceConfiguration.endpoint,InferenceConfiguration.modelName
  reads InferenceConfiguration.endpoint,InferenceConfiguration.modelName,InferenceConfiguration.allowRemote
  writes InferenceConfiguration.endpoint,InferenceConfiguration.modelName,InferenceConfiguration.allowRemote,InferenceConfiguration.updatedAt
  ensure ConfigureAndroidModel.remote_consent statement "A non-loopback endpoint is persisted only with allowRemote=true." refs InferenceConfiguration.endpoint,InferenceConfiguration.allowRemote
  ensure ConfigureAndroidModel.dedicated_screen statement "Endpoint, model, consent explanation, and save action are presented on a separate navigable screen rather than a transient dialog on the gallery screen." refs InferenceConfiguration.endpoint,InferenceConfiguration.modelName,InferenceConfiguration.allowRemote
  ensure ConfigureAndroidModel.local_identity_route statement "The dedicated settings screen directs both person and pet registration to the separate local identity screen and does not collect Android VLM identity candidates." refs InferenceConfiguration.endpoint
  reject ConfigureAndroidModel.remote_without_consent statement "Saving a non-loopback endpoint without explicit consent is rejected." refs InferenceConfiguration.endpoint,InferenceConfiguration.allowRemote
  sideeffect ConfigureAndroidModel.local_settings_only statement "Configuration writes only app-private preferences and sends no photo." refs InferenceConfiguration.updatedAt
  idempotency "Saving the same valid values preserves the same effective inference configuration."
  forbid ConfigureAndroidModel.no_request_on_save statement "Saving settings must not upload or annotate any photo." refs InferenceConfiguration.endpoint

function ScanAndroidGalleryFunctionPromise action scan:
  label "扫描 Android 相册 Function Promise"
  summary "Reads permission-visible MediaStore images, hashes original content streams, and refreshes the app-private catalog."
  depends PhotoAssetFieldPromise,AndroidMediaLocationFieldPromise,FaceTemplateFieldPromise,FaceObservationFieldPromise,PetTemplateFieldPromise,PetObservationFieldPromise
  trigger "User grants Android photo permission and invokes scan."
  precondition ScanAndroidGallery.permission statement "Android has granted full or selected-photo read access." refs AndroidMediaLocation.accessible
  reads AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.mediaStoreId,AndroidMediaLocation.modifiedSeconds,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible
  writes PhotoAsset.id,PhotoAsset.mediaType,PhotoAsset.byteSize,PhotoAsset.discoveredAt,AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.mediaStoreId,AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,AndroidMediaLocation.displayName,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,AndroidMediaLocation.modifiedSeconds,AndroidMediaLocation.lastSeenAt
  ensure ScanAndroidGallery.content_hash statement "Every newly observed or changed URI is identified by streaming SHA-256 over ContentResolver bytes." refs PhotoAsset.id,AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,AndroidMediaLocation.uri
  ensure ScanAndroidGallery.permission_scoped_visibility statement "Previously cataloged URIs not visible in this scan become accessible=false without deletion claims." refs AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,AndroidMediaLocation.lastSeenAt
  ensure ScanAndroidGallery.partial_reselection statement "On Android 14 or later, if access is partial, every user scan action launches the system selected-photo permission flow before querying MediaStore." refs AndroidMediaLocation.accessible
  ensure ScanAndroidGallery.local_face_index statement "When at least one person template exists, every newly visible unindexed photo is passed to the bundled local detector and embedding matcher after catalog scan." refs FaceTemplate.identityId,FaceObservation.photoId,FaceObservation.modelName
  ensure ScanAndroidGallery.local_pet_index statement "When at least one pet template exists, every newly visible unindexed photo is passed to the bundled local cat-and-dog detector and pet embedding matcher after catalog scan." refs PetTemplate.identityId,PetObservation.photoId,PetObservation.modelName
  sideeffect ScanAndroidGallery.catalog_only statement "Only the app-private SQLite catalog changes." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri
  idempotency "An unchanged permission-visible MediaStore snapshot keeps content identities and reuses hashes for unchanged metadata."
  forbid ScanAndroidGallery.no_media_mutation statement "Never update, move, rename, trash, or delete a MediaStore item." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri

function BrowseAndroidPhotoWallFunctionPromise action browse:
  label "浏览 Android 按日照片墙 Function Promise"
  summary "Shows a startup-only story introduction, then loads every distinct currently accessible photo into a compact lazy day-grouped photo-wall page with a bottom Dock ordered heatmap, people, Agent search, settings-rightmost, and renders a separate one-screen vertically chronological heatmap page whose borderless full-area grid is fused with vertical year/granularity side controls and GitHub-style annual daily, weekly, and monthly views from exact daily counts."
  depends AndroidMediaLocationFieldPromise,AndroidPhotoWallFieldPromise,PhotoAnnotationFieldPromise
  trigger "The photo-wall or dedicated heatmap page opens, the user right-swipes on the photo wall or taps its heatmap action, accessible catalog state changes, the display mode or heatmap granularity changes, the displayed year changes, or the user selects or clears a heatmap range."
  precondition BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.catalog_available statement "The app-private catalog may be empty, but any projected row must have one currently accessible MediaStore location." refs AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible
  reads AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.displayName,AndroidMediaLocation.dateTakenMillis,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,PhotoAnnotation.photoId,PhotoAnnotation.caption,PhotoAnnotation.tags,PhotoAnnotation.facets,PhotoAnnotation.createdAt
  writes AndroidPhotoWall.photoIds,AndroidPhotoWall.dayGroups,AndroidPhotoWall.displayMode,AndroidPhotoWall.displayedYear,AndroidPhotoWall.heatmapGranularity,AndroidPhotoWall.selectedRange,AndroidPhotoWall.dailyCounts
  ensure BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.all_accessible_photos statement "The wall query has no search-result limit, includes annotated and unannotated photos, chooses one currently accessible URI per distinct photoId, and excludes inaccessible locations." refs AndroidPhotoWall.photoIds,AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible
  ensure BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.day_sections statement "Photos are grouped by device-local date derived only from dateTakenMillis, dated groups and photos are newest first, and null capture times appear once in a final unknown-time group." refs AndroidPhotoWall.dayGroups,AndroidMediaLocation.dateTakenMillis
  ensure BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.thumbnail_mode statement "Thumbnail mode renders a lazy three-column square grid with one tappable thumbnail per projected photo." refs AndroidPhotoWall.displayMode,AndroidPhotoWall.photoIds
  ensure BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.detail_mode statement "Detail mode renders the same photos in the same order as full-width cards and shows annotation content only when a latest annotation exists." refs AndroidPhotoWall.displayMode,AndroidPhotoWall.photoIds,PhotoAnnotation.caption
  ensure BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.dedicated_pages statement "The photo wall and annual heatmap are separate native pages: the photo-wall page shows no annual heatmap, exposes a bottom Dock heatmap action and a right-swipe route, the heatmap page shows no photo cards, and a selected-range action from heatmap opens the photo-wall page without changing the exact range." refs AndroidPhotoWall.selectedRange,AndroidPhotoWall.dayGroups
  ensure BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.annual_heatmaps statement "The dedicated heatmap page fits the complete annual grid in one screen without a page scroll; its vertically stacked side controls are part of the same borderless full-area composition and navigate natural calendar years or switch day, week, and month views. Day mode renders every Sunday-through-Saturday week as one compact row in chronological vertical order; week mode renders every 53 or 54 intersecting calendar week as one compact chronological vertical row; month mode renders all twelve calendar months as chronological vertical rows. The grid expands through the available content area instead of sitting in a standalone card. All modes use GitHub's square green five-level visual grammar, a 少-to-多 guide, selected-range emphasis, exact counts, and complete accessible range descriptions." refs AndroidPhotoWall.displayedYear,AndroidPhotoWall.heatmapGranularity,AndroidPhotoWall.selectedRange,AndroidPhotoWall.dailyCounts
  ensure BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.range_filter statement "Tapping a non-empty daily, weekly, or monthly cell selects exactly the real capture-day groups in that inclusive cell range, shows the exact selected range and count on the heatmap page, offers a visible action to view the selection on the photo-wall page, and a clear action restores all groups." refs AndroidPhotoWall.displayedYear,AndroidPhotoWall.heatmapGranularity,AndroidPhotoWall.selectedRange,AndroidPhotoWall.dayGroups,AndroidPhotoWall.dailyCounts
  reject BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.inaccessible statement "A photo without a currently accessible MediaStore location is absent even if an annotation remains." refs AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,PhotoAnnotation.photoId
  sideeffect BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.read_only statement "Browsing reads the catalog and thumbnails only; page, display, aggregation, and selection state remain app-local and do not mutate MediaStore or annotation history." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidPhotoWall.displayMode,AndroidPhotoWall.displayedYear,AndroidPhotoWall.heatmapGranularity,AndroidPhotoWall.selectedRange
  idempotency "The same accessible catalog, device time zone, page, display mode, displayed year, heatmap granularity, and selected range produce the same membership, groups, counts, levels, and stable order."
  forbid BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.no_date_fallback statement "Modified time, discovery time, index time, and annotation time cannot stand in for a missing capture timestamp." refs AndroidMediaLocation.dateTakenMillis,PhotoAnnotation.createdAt

function ViewAndroidPhotoFunctionPromise action view:
  label "在 APM 内查看照片 Function Promise"
  summary "Opens the tapped accessible photo in APM's native full-screen viewer, decodes its complete original image resolution, supports original-pixel zoom and bounded pan, and navigates the stable accessible-photo sequence."
  depends AndroidMediaLocationFieldPromise,AndroidPhotoWallFieldPromise,AndroidPhotoViewerFieldPromise
  trigger "The user taps an accessible photo in the photo wall, text search, Agent search, or similar-photo results, or selects previous or next inside the viewer."
  precondition ViewAndroidPhoto.accessible_photo statement "The requested photoId maps to a currently accessible URI in the app-private catalog." refs AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible
  reads AndroidPhotoWall.photoIds,AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.displayName,AndroidMediaLocation.dateTakenMillis,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible
  writes AndroidPhotoViewer.photoIds,AndroidPhotoViewer.selectedPhotoId,AndroidPhotoViewer.displayBitmap,AndroidPhotoViewer.zoomScale,AndroidPhotoViewer.panOffset
  ensure ViewAndroidPhoto.in_app_destination statement "Opening from every APM photo-result surface starts the private native PhotoViewerActivity and keeps the user inside APM rather than resolving an external image application." refs AndroidPhotoViewer.selectedPhotoId,AndroidMediaLocation.uri
  ensure ViewAndroidPhoto.exact_initial_selection statement "The first selectedPhotoId equals the exact accessible photoId tapped by the user, even when it originated in search or similarity results." refs AndroidPhotoViewer.selectedPhotoId,AndroidMediaLocation.photoId
  ensure ViewAndroidPhoto.aspect_fit statement "The selected original URI is decoded off the main thread with ImageDecoder at its complete orientation-correct intrinsic dimensions and preserved aspect ratio, then shown fully fit on a dark full-screen surface at scale 1 without a thumbnail request or target size." refs AndroidPhotoViewer.displayBitmap,AndroidPhotoViewer.zoomScale
  ensure ViewAndroidPhoto.zoom_and_pan statement "Pinch gestures clamp scale from 1 through max(5, nativePixelScale), permitting at least one original pixel per display pixel; pan remains bounded while zoomed, and changing selectedPhotoId resets scale and pan before rendering that photo." refs AndroidPhotoViewer.zoomScale,AndroidPhotoViewer.panOffset,AndroidPhotoViewer.selectedPhotoId
  ensure ViewAndroidPhoto.adjacent_navigation statement "Visible previous and next controls move by one through the stable accessible wall order, disable at sequence boundaries, and show the current one-based position and total count." refs AndroidPhotoViewer.photoIds,AndroidPhotoViewer.selectedPhotoId
  reject ViewAndroidPhoto.inaccessible_or_unreadable statement "A missing, newly inaccessible, or undecodable URI shows an in-app error state and never falls back to an external viewer or fabricates image content." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,AndroidPhotoViewer.displayBitmap
  sideeffect ViewAndroidPhoto.read_only statement "The function reads the app-private catalog and selected content URI only; navigation and gesture state are ephemeral and no MediaStore or annotation row is written." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidPhotoViewer.selectedPhotoId,AndroidPhotoViewer.zoomScale,AndroidPhotoViewer.panOffset
  idempotency "Opening the same accessible photo against the same catalog order selects the same item and decodes the same complete original dimensions; gesture state always starts at scale 1 and zero pan."
  forbid ViewAndroidPhoto.no_external_view statement "No viewer entry point constructs or dispatches Intent.ACTION_VIEW for a photo URI." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidPhotoViewer.selectedPhotoId

function SelectAndroidPhotosForAnnotationFunctionPromise action select:
  label "选择 Android 待标注照片 Function Promise"
  summary "Uses the Android system multi-photo picker to grant read access, catalog only the returned URIs, and replace the selected-photo annotation scope."
  depends PhotoAssetFieldPromise,AndroidMediaLocationFieldPromise,AndroidAnnotationSelectionFieldPromise
  trigger "User taps 选择照片 and completes the Android system photo picker."
  precondition SelectAndroidPhotosForAnnotation.system_result statement "The returned URI list comes from the registered Android system photo-picker contract." refs AndroidAnnotationSelection.source
  reads AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,AndroidAnnotationSelection.photoIds
  writes PhotoAsset.id,PhotoAsset.mediaType,PhotoAsset.byteSize,PhotoAsset.discoveredAt,AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.mediaStoreId,AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,AndroidMediaLocation.displayName,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,AndroidMediaLocation.modifiedSeconds,AndroidMediaLocation.lastSeenAt,AndroidAnnotationSelection.photoIds,AndroidAnnotationSelection.selectedAt
  ensure SelectAndroidPhotosForAnnotation.content_hash statement "Every returned readable URI is content-addressed by streaming SHA-256 without modifying the original." refs PhotoAsset.id,AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.photoId
  ensure SelectAndroidPhotosForAnnotation.exact_scope statement "After a non-empty picker result, photoIds contains exactly the deduplicated readable selected photos and no previously selected extras." refs AndroidAnnotationSelection.photoIds,AndroidAnnotationSelection.selectedAt
  ensure SelectAndroidPhotosForAnnotation.preserve_other_access statement "Cataloging a selected set does not mark other previously authorized locations inaccessible." refs AndroidMediaLocation.accessible
  reject SelectAndroidPhotosForAnnotation.cancelled statement "A cancelled or empty picker result starts no annotation and does not silently select the full library." refs AndroidAnnotationSelection.photoIds
  reject SelectAndroidPhotosForAnnotation.unreadable statement "An unreadable returned URI is excluded, reported, and never sent to a model." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible
  sideeffect SelectAndroidPhotosForAnnotation.catalog_and_selection_only statement "Only picker grants, app-private catalog rows, and the app-private selection set change." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidAnnotationSelection.photoIds
  idempotency "Selecting the same unchanged URI set preserves content identities and replaces the selection with the same deduplicated photo IDs."
  forbid SelectAndroidPhotosForAnnotation.no_media_mutation statement "Never update, move, rename, trash, or delete a selected source photo." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri

function RegisterPersonIdentityFunctionPromise action register:
  label "注册本地人物 Function Promise"
  summary "Uses Android Photo Picker, detects faces locally, lets the user tap exactly one face and name it, then stores only its embedding template."
  depends AndroidMediaLocationFieldPromise,PersonIdentityFieldPromise,FaceTemplateFieldPromise,FaceObservationFieldPromise
  trigger "User opens local person recognition, chooses a reference photo, taps one detected face, enters a name, and saves."
  precondition RegisterPersonIdentity.reference_readable statement "The picker-granted content URI is readable for this registration operation." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri
  precondition RegisterPersonIdentity.face_selected statement "At least one quality-eligible face is detected and the user explicitly taps exactly one bounding box." refs FaceTemplate.boundingBox
  precondition RegisterPersonIdentity.valid_name statement "The trimmed name is non-empty, length-bounded, and compatible with unique local identity labels." refs PersonIdentity.name
  reads AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,PersonIdentity.name,FaceTemplate.modelName
  writes PersonIdentity.id,PersonIdentity.name,PersonIdentity.createdAt,PersonIdentity.updatedAt,FaceTemplate.id,FaceTemplate.identityId,FaceTemplate.embedding,FaceTemplate.dimension,FaceTemplate.modelName,FaceTemplate.sourcePhotoId,FaceTemplate.boundingBox,FaceTemplate.createdAt,FaceObservation.matchState,FaceObservation.matchedIdentityId,FaceObservation.similarity
  ensure RegisterPersonIdentity.selected_embedding statement "Only the tapped face is aligned, cropped in memory, embedded, L2-normalized, and associated with the entered identity." refs FaceTemplate.identityId,FaceTemplate.embedding,FaceTemplate.boundingBox
  ensure RegisterPersonIdentity.scale_robust_reference statement "A clear quality-eligible frontal face remains detectable when it fills most of the reference photo because at least one bounded downscaled detector pass keeps it within the detector's trained face-size range." refs FaceTemplate.boundingBox,FaceTemplate.embedding
  ensure RegisterPersonIdentity.local_only statement "Face detection, alignment, embedding, template storage, and rematching run on device without any HTTP request." refs FaceTemplate.embedding,FaceObservation.embedding
  ensure RegisterPersonIdentity.rematch_existing statement "After a template is added, stored observations are rematched so already scanned annotated photos can become searchable by the identity name without another VLM call." refs FaceObservation.matchedIdentityId,FaceObservation.similarity
  reject RegisterPersonIdentity.no_face statement "A reference with no quality-eligible face after all required detection scales creates no identity or template, and the UI does not falsely claim that the face was necessarily too small." refs FaceTemplate.id,FaceTemplate.boundingBox
  reject RegisterPersonIdentity.no_selection statement "A detected face that the user did not tap cannot be registered." refs FaceTemplate.boundingBox
  reject RegisterPersonIdentity.invalid_embedding statement "A missing, non-finite, wrong-dimension, or zero-norm embedding creates no template." refs FaceTemplate.embedding,FaceTemplate.dimension
  sideeffect RegisterPersonIdentity.private_biometric_store statement "Only app-private identity, template, and derived match rows change; original and reference photo bytes remain unchanged." refs PersonIdentity.id,FaceTemplate.id
  idempotency "Registering another valid reference under the same normalized name appends a template to that identity rather than creating a duplicate identity."
  forbid RegisterPersonIdentity.no_reference_retention statement "Never store the picked bitmap, aligned face crop, image bytes, or upload the template." refs FaceTemplate.embedding,FaceTemplate.sourcePhotoId

function MatchAndroidFacesFunctionPromise action match:
  label "本地匹配相册人脸 Function Promise"
  summary "Detects faces in accessible photos, extracts local embeddings, and records only thresholded unambiguous identity matches; every other face is unknown."
  depends AndroidMediaLocationFieldPromise,PersonIdentityFieldPromise,FaceTemplateFieldPromise,FaceObservationFieldPromise
  trigger "A scan discovers an unindexed accessible photo, registration changes templates, or annotation requests current local identities."
  precondition MatchAndroidFaces.accessible statement "Only a currently permission-accessible content URI is read for first-time detection." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible
  reads AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,PersonIdentity.id,PersonIdentity.name,FaceTemplate.identityId,FaceTemplate.embedding,FaceTemplate.dimension,FaceTemplate.modelName,FaceObservation.embedding,FaceObservation.modelName
  writes FaceObservation.id,FaceObservation.photoId,FaceObservation.faceIndex,FaceObservation.embedding,FaceObservation.boundingBox,FaceObservation.detectorScore,FaceObservation.modelName,FaceObservation.pipelineVersion,FaceObservation.matchState,FaceObservation.matchedIdentityId,FaceObservation.similarity,FaceObservation.threshold,FaceObservation.indexedAt
  ensure MatchAndroidFaces.local_embedding statement "Detection, five-landmark alignment, cropping, and embedding run with bundled models on device and never call the VLM endpoint." refs FaceObservation.embedding,FaceObservation.modelName
  ensure MatchAndroidFaces.multiscale_coverage statement "Bounded detector passes cover large close-up faces and smaller distant faces, map boxes and five landmarks back to one original coordinate space, and use original-resolution pixels for alignment and embedding." refs FaceObservation.boundingBox,FaceObservation.embedding,FaceObservation.detectorScore
  ensure MatchAndroidFaces.cross_scale_dedup statement "Cross-scale overlap suppression emits one observation per physical face in stable spatial order." refs FaceObservation.faceIndex,FaceObservation.boundingBox,FaceObservation.detectorScore
  ensure MatchAndroidFaces.pipeline_reindex statement "Changing detector scale or deduplication behavior changes the face-index pipeline version so photos previously recorded with zero or stale detections are eligible for automatic re-indexing without invalidating compatible registered embeddings." refs FaceObservation.pipelineVersion,FaceObservation.indexedAt,FaceTemplate.modelName
  ensure MatchAndroidFaces.threshold_and_margin statement "A person is accepted only when the best cosine similarity is at least 0.55 and exceeds the best different identity by at least 0.05." refs FaceObservation.similarity,FaceObservation.threshold,FaceObservation.matchedIdentityId
  ensure MatchAndroidFaces.unknown_by_default statement "No templates, low similarity, ambiguous candidates, invalid faces, and unmatched faces produce unknown with no identity name." refs FaceObservation.matchState,FaceObservation.matchedIdentityId
  ensure MatchAndroidFaces.current_provenance statement "Each indexed photo records zero-face completion or one observation per detected face for the current detector and embedding model version." refs FaceObservation.photoId,FaceObservation.faceIndex,FaceObservation.modelName,FaceObservation.indexedAt
  reject MatchAndroidFaces.inaccessible statement "No new photo pixels are read when the MediaStore URI is not currently accessible." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible
  reject MatchAndroidFaces.invalid_embedding statement "Non-finite, wrong-dimension, or zero-norm embeddings are not matched or persisted as identities." refs FaceObservation.embedding
  sideeffect MatchAndroidFaces.local_database_only statement "Only app-private face index and derived match rows change." refs FaceObservation.id,FaceObservation.matchedIdentityId
  idempotency "A photo already indexed with the same content hash and face model is not re-read; template changes rematch stored embeddings only."
  forbid MatchAndroidFaces.no_vlm_person_decision statement "VLM captions, prompts, candidate names, and responses cannot influence person match scores or identity decisions." refs FaceObservation.matchState,FaceObservation.matchedIdentityId

function RegisterPetIdentityFunctionPromise action register:
  label "注册本地宠物 Function Promise"
  summary "Uses Android Photo Picker, detects cats and dogs locally, lets the user tap exactly one detected pet and name it, then stores only its visual embedding template."
  depends AndroidMediaLocationFieldPromise,PetIdentityFieldPromise,PetTemplateFieldPromise,PetObservationFieldPromise
  trigger "User opens local identity recognition, selects pet mode, chooses a reference photo, taps one detected cat or dog, enters a name, and saves."
  precondition RegisterPetIdentity.reference_readable statement "The picker-granted content URI is readable for this registration operation." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri
  precondition RegisterPetIdentity.pet_selected statement "At least one quality-eligible cat or dog is locally detected and the user explicitly taps exactly one bounding box." refs PetTemplate.boundingBox,PetTemplate.species
  precondition RegisterPetIdentity.valid_name statement "The trimmed pet name is non-empty, length-bounded, and compatible with unique local pet labels." refs PetIdentity.name
  reads AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,PetIdentity.name,PetTemplate.modelName,PetTemplate.species
  writes PetIdentity.id,PetIdentity.name,PetIdentity.createdAt,PetIdentity.updatedAt,PetTemplate.id,PetTemplate.identityId,PetTemplate.species,PetTemplate.embedding,PetTemplate.dimension,PetTemplate.modelName,PetTemplate.sourcePhotoId,PetTemplate.boundingBox,PetTemplate.createdAt,PetObservation.matchState,PetObservation.matchedIdentityId,PetObservation.similarity
  ensure RegisterPetIdentity.selected_embedding statement "Only the tapped pet crop is embedded in memory, L2-normalized, and associated with the entered pet identity and detected species." refs PetTemplate.identityId,PetTemplate.species,PetTemplate.embedding,PetTemplate.boundingBox
  ensure RegisterPetIdentity.local_only statement "Pet detection, cropping, embedding, template storage, and rematching run on device without any HTTP request." refs PetTemplate.embedding,PetObservation.embedding
  ensure RegisterPetIdentity.rematch_existing statement "After a pet template is added, stored same-species observations are rematched so already annotated photos can become searchable by the pet name without another VLM call." refs PetObservation.matchedIdentityId,PetObservation.similarity
  reject RegisterPetIdentity.no_pet statement "A reference with no quality-eligible cat or dog creates no identity or template and reports the supported categories clearly." refs PetTemplate.id,PetTemplate.boundingBox
  reject RegisterPetIdentity.no_selection statement "A detected pet that the user did not tap cannot be registered." refs PetTemplate.boundingBox
  reject RegisterPetIdentity.invalid_embedding statement "A missing, non-finite, wrong-dimension, or zero-norm pet embedding creates no template." refs PetTemplate.embedding,PetTemplate.dimension
  sideeffect RegisterPetIdentity.private_template_store statement "Only app-private identity, template, and derived match rows change; original and reference photo bytes remain unchanged." refs PetIdentity.id,PetTemplate.id
  idempotency "Registering another valid reference under the same normalized pet name appends a template to that pet identity rather than creating a duplicate."
  forbid RegisterPetIdentity.no_reference_retention statement "Never store the picked bitmap, pet crop, image bytes, or upload the template." refs PetTemplate.embedding,PetTemplate.sourcePhotoId

function MatchAndroidPetsFunctionPromise action match:
  label "本地匹配相册宠物 Function Promise"
  summary "Detects cats and dogs in accessible photos, extracts local visual embeddings, and records only conservative same-species unambiguous identity matches; every other pet is unknown."
  depends AndroidMediaLocationFieldPromise,PetIdentityFieldPromise,PetTemplateFieldPromise,PetObservationFieldPromise
  trigger "A scan discovers an unindexed accessible photo, pet registration changes templates, or annotation requests current local identities."
  precondition MatchAndroidPets.accessible statement "Only a currently permission-accessible content URI is read for first-time detection." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible
  reads AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,PetIdentity.id,PetIdentity.name,PetTemplate.identityId,PetTemplate.species,PetTemplate.embedding,PetTemplate.dimension,PetTemplate.modelName,PetObservation.embedding,PetObservation.modelName
  writes PetObservation.id,PetObservation.photoId,PetObservation.petIndex,PetObservation.species,PetObservation.embedding,PetObservation.boundingBox,PetObservation.detectorScore,PetObservation.modelName,PetObservation.pipelineVersion,PetObservation.matchState,PetObservation.matchedIdentityId,PetObservation.similarity,PetObservation.threshold,PetObservation.indexedAt
  ensure MatchAndroidPets.local_embedding statement "Detection, padded cropping, and embedding run with bundled models on device and never call the VLM endpoint." refs PetObservation.embedding,PetObservation.modelName
  ensure MatchAndroidPets.same_species_only statement "Cat observations compare only with cat templates and dog observations compare only with dog templates." refs PetObservation.species,PetObservation.matchedIdentityId,PetTemplate.species
  ensure MatchAndroidPets.threshold_and_margin statement "A pet is accepted only when the best cosine similarity is at least 0.90 and exceeds the best different same-species identity by at least 0.04." refs PetObservation.similarity,PetObservation.threshold,PetObservation.matchedIdentityId
  ensure MatchAndroidPets.unknown_by_default statement "No templates, low similarity, ambiguity, unsupported species, invalid crops, and unmatched pets produce unknown with no identity name." refs PetObservation.matchState,PetObservation.matchedIdentityId
  ensure MatchAndroidPets.current_provenance statement "Each indexed photo records zero-pet completion or one observation per detected cat or dog for the current detector and embedding pipeline version." refs PetObservation.photoId,PetObservation.petIndex,PetObservation.modelName,PetObservation.pipelineVersion,PetObservation.indexedAt
  reject MatchAndroidPets.inaccessible statement "No new photo pixels are read when the MediaStore URI is not currently accessible." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible
  reject MatchAndroidPets.invalid_embedding statement "Non-finite, wrong-dimension, or zero-norm embeddings are not matched or persisted as identities." refs PetObservation.embedding
  sideeffect MatchAndroidPets.local_database_only statement "Only app-private pet index and derived match rows change." refs PetObservation.id,PetObservation.matchedIdentityId
  idempotency "A photo already indexed with the same content hash and pet pipeline is not re-read; template changes rematch stored embeddings only."
  forbid MatchAndroidPets.no_vlm_pet_decision statement "VLM captions, prompts, candidate names, and responses cannot influence pet match scores or identity decisions." refs PetObservation.matchState,PetObservation.matchedIdentityId

function CheckAndroidVisualSimilarityFunctionPromise action check:
  label "触发 Android 相似检查 Function Promise"
  summary "The 检查相似 button requires one explicit scope, refreshes MediaStore visibility, and delegates only that scope to the local DINOv2 visual indexer."
  depends SimilarityCheckRequestFieldPromise,AndroidMediaLocationFieldPromise,PhotoVisualFeatureFieldPromise,GeneralSubjectObservationFieldPromise
  trigger "User taps 检查相似, chooses 增量检查, 近期检查, or 全量检查, supplies a valid custom duration when required, and confirms."
  precondition CheckAndroidVisualSimilarity.explicit_scope statement "Exactly one valid SimilarityCheckRequest is confirmed before permission or indexing work begins." refs SimilarityCheckRequest.mode,SimilarityCheckRequest.recentAmount,SimilarityCheckRequest.recentUnit,SimilarityCheckRequest.requestedAtMillis,SimilarityCheckRequest.recentCutoffMillis
  precondition CheckAndroidVisualSimilarity.model_available statement "The checksum-verified bundled DINOv2 model is available before the check starts." refs PhotoVisualFeature.modelName,PhotoVisualFeature.pipelineVersion
  reads SimilarityCheckRequest.mode,SimilarityCheckRequest.recentAmount,SimilarityCheckRequest.recentUnit,SimilarityCheckRequest.requestedAtMillis,SimilarityCheckRequest.recentCutoffMillis,AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.dateTakenMillis,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,PhotoVisualFeature.photoId,PhotoVisualFeature.modelName,PhotoVisualFeature.pipelineVersion
  writes PhotoVisualFeature.photoId,PhotoVisualFeature.globalEmbedding,PhotoVisualFeature.dimension,PhotoVisualFeature.patchGrid,PhotoVisualFeature.gridSize,PhotoVisualFeature.modelName,PhotoVisualFeature.pipelineVersion,PhotoVisualFeature.indexedAt,GeneralSubjectObservation.id,GeneralSubjectObservation.photoId,GeneralSubjectObservation.subjectIndex,GeneralSubjectObservation.category,GeneralSubjectObservation.embedding,GeneralSubjectObservation.dimension,GeneralSubjectObservation.boundingBox,GeneralSubjectObservation.detectorScore,GeneralSubjectObservation.detectorName,GeneralSubjectObservation.modelName,GeneralSubjectObservation.pipelineVersion,GeneralSubjectObservation.indexedAt
  ensure CheckAndroidVisualSimilarity.one_button_three_modes statement "The primary screen exposes one 检查相似 button whose confirmation surface visibly offers incremental new-photo, custom recent, and full-library checks." refs SimilarityCheckRequest.mode,SimilarityCheckRequest.recentAmount,SimilarityCheckRequest.recentUnit
  ensure CheckAndroidVisualSimilarity.refresh_visibility statement "Every confirmed mode first refreshes the currently authorized MediaStore snapshot; Android 14 partial access reopens reselection before scanning." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,AndroidMediaLocation.lastSeenAt
  ensure CheckAndroidVisualSimilarity.incremental_scope statement "Incremental mode processes only currently accessible content lacking the exact current model and pipeline feature, so newly discovered and previously unfinished photos are added without recomputing current photos." refs SimilarityCheckRequest.mode,AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,PhotoVisualFeature.photoId,PhotoVisualFeature.modelName,PhotoVisualFeature.pipelineVersion
  ensure CheckAndroidVisualSimilarity.recent_scope statement "Recent mode recomputes every currently accessible photo whose real MediaStore dateTakenMillis is at or after the user-derived cutoff, including photos already indexed by the current pipeline." refs SimilarityCheckRequest.mode,SimilarityCheckRequest.recentCutoffMillis,AndroidMediaLocation.dateTakenMillis,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,PhotoVisualFeature.indexedAt
  ensure CheckAndroidVisualSimilarity.full_scope statement "Full mode recomputes every currently accessible photo with no hidden count limit, including photos already indexed by the current pipeline." refs SimilarityCheckRequest.mode,AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,PhotoVisualFeature.indexedAt
  ensure CheckAndroidVisualSimilarity.scope_report statement "Progress and completion visibly report selected mode, considered photos, successful refreshes, failures, and recent photos excluded because capture time is unavailable." refs SimilarityCheckRequest.mode,AndroidMediaLocation.dateTakenMillis,PhotoVisualFeature.indexedAt
  reject CheckAndroidVisualSimilarity.invalid_recent statement "A recent request with invalid amount, unit, cutoff, or missing capture time never expands to a broader photo scope; unknown capture-time photos are counted as excluded." refs SimilarityCheckRequest.recentAmount,SimilarityCheckRequest.recentUnit,SimilarityCheckRequest.recentCutoffMillis,AndroidMediaLocation.dateTakenMillis
  reject CheckAndroidVisualSimilarity.inaccessible statement "No photo outside current permission-visible MediaStore state is decoded or indexed." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible
  sideeffect CheckAndroidVisualSimilarity.derived_only statement "Only app-private catalog visibility and derived visual feature rows change; originals are read-only and no network request occurs." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,PhotoVisualFeature.globalEmbedding,GeneralSubjectObservation.embedding
  idempotency "Incremental mode converges to zero pending current-pipeline photos; repeated recent or full checks replace each successful derived feature atomically rather than adding duplicate rows."
  forbid CheckAndroidVisualSimilarity.no_predelete statement "A forced recent or full check never deletes a prior valid feature before a replacement for that photo has been fully computed and committed." refs PhotoVisualFeature.photoId,PhotoVisualFeature.indexedAt

function IndexAndroidVisualSimilarityFunctionPromise action index:
  label "索引 Android 视觉相似特征 Function Promise"
  summary "Uses the public DINOv2 ViT-S/14 registers checkpoint on device to index normalized whole-photo and 4x4 spatial vectors, then reuses local face and pet observations and embeds quality-eligible general subject crops."
  depends AndroidMediaLocationFieldPromise,PhotoVisualFeatureFieldPromise,FaceObservationFieldPromise,PetObservationFieldPromise,GeneralSubjectObservationFieldPromise
  trigger "A validated similarity check supplies an explicit photo scope, a newly accessible photo lacks the current pipeline, or the DINOv2 pipeline version changes."
  precondition IndexAndroidVisualSimilarity.accessible statement "Only currently permission-accessible content URIs are decoded." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible
  precondition IndexAndroidVisualSimilarity.model_available statement "The exact public DINOv2 ViT-S/14 registers checkpoint is present in app-private or packaged model storage and passes its expected SHA-256 identity check before indexing." refs PhotoVisualFeature.modelName,PhotoVisualFeature.pipelineVersion
  reads AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,FaceObservation.photoId,FaceObservation.embedding,FaceObservation.boundingBox,PetObservation.photoId,PetObservation.embedding,PetObservation.boundingBox
  writes PhotoVisualFeature.photoId,PhotoVisualFeature.globalEmbedding,PhotoVisualFeature.dimension,PhotoVisualFeature.patchGrid,PhotoVisualFeature.gridSize,PhotoVisualFeature.modelName,PhotoVisualFeature.pipelineVersion,PhotoVisualFeature.indexedAt,GeneralSubjectObservation.id,GeneralSubjectObservation.photoId,GeneralSubjectObservation.subjectIndex,GeneralSubjectObservation.category,GeneralSubjectObservation.embedding,GeneralSubjectObservation.dimension,GeneralSubjectObservation.boundingBox,GeneralSubjectObservation.detectorScore,GeneralSubjectObservation.detectorName,GeneralSubjectObservation.modelName,GeneralSubjectObservation.pipelineVersion,GeneralSubjectObservation.indexedAt
  ensure IndexAndroidVisualSimilarity.dinov2_global statement "One bounded orientation-corrected in-memory thumbnail produces a finite L2-normalized 384-dimensional DINOv2 class-token descriptor from an exact [1,261,384] model output." refs PhotoVisualFeature.globalEmbedding,PhotoVisualFeature.dimension,PhotoVisualFeature.modelName
  ensure IndexAndroidVisualSimilarity.four_by_four_patches statement "After excluding one class and four register tokens, the 16x16 DINOv2 patch tokens are pooled by original coordinates into exactly sixteen row-major 4x4 cells and every cell is normalized independently." refs PhotoVisualFeature.patchGrid,PhotoVisualFeature.gridSize,PhotoVisualFeature.dimension
  ensure IndexAndroidVisualSimilarity.general_subject_crops statement "The bundled local object detector selects a bounded number of quality-eligible non-person, non-cat, non-dog subjects; padded crops are embedded by the same DINOv2 checkpoint and discarded immediately." refs GeneralSubjectObservation.category,GeneralSubjectObservation.embedding,GeneralSubjectObservation.boundingBox
  ensure IndexAndroidVisualSimilarity.reuse_identity_observations statement "Person and pet subject evidence reuses existing local FaceObservation and PetObservation embeddings and bounds rather than duplicating detections in the general-subject table." refs FaceObservation.embedding,FaceObservation.boundingBox,PetObservation.embedding,PetObservation.boundingBox,GeneralSubjectObservation.category
  ensure IndexAndroidVisualSimilarity.provenance statement "Every committed feature records content identity, exact checkpoint, detector, preprocessing, pooling, quantization, and successful index time." refs PhotoVisualFeature.photoId,PhotoVisualFeature.modelName,PhotoVisualFeature.pipelineVersion,PhotoVisualFeature.indexedAt,GeneralSubjectObservation.detectorName,GeneralSubjectObservation.modelName,GeneralSubjectObservation.pipelineVersion
  ensure IndexAndroidVisualSimilarity.resumable statement "Incremental scope skips a photo already indexed by the same content identity and pipeline; explicit recent or full scopes may atomically replace it, while every failure remains retryable without erasing an older valid feature." refs PhotoVisualFeature.photoId,PhotoVisualFeature.pipelineVersion,PhotoVisualFeature.indexedAt
  reject IndexAndroidVisualSimilarity.inaccessible statement "No photo pixels are read when current MediaStore permission is absent." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible
  reject IndexAndroidVisualSimilarity.missing_model statement "A missing, wrong, or checksum-mismatched DINOv2 model writes no visual or subject feature and reports a visible actionable error." refs PhotoVisualFeature.modelName,PhotoVisualFeature.pipelineVersion
  reject IndexAndroidVisualSimilarity.invalid_output statement "Wrong dimensions, non-finite values, empty vectors, missing patch cells, or zero norms commit no partial feature set for that photo." refs PhotoVisualFeature.globalEmbedding,PhotoVisualFeature.patchGrid,GeneralSubjectObservation.embedding
  sideeffect IndexAndroidVisualSimilarity.local_database_only statement "Only app-private derived feature rows change; thumbnails and crops stay in memory, no HTTP request occurs, and MediaStore originals remain unchanged." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,PhotoVisualFeature.globalEmbedding,GeneralSubjectObservation.embedding
  idempotency "The same content hash, checkpoint, and pipeline produces one atomically replaceable derived feature set rather than duplicate rows, regardless of how many explicit checks run."
  forbid IndexAndroidVisualSimilarity.no_vlm_features statement "Neither VLM output nor annotation state can create, alter, or fill missing visual vectors." refs PhotoVisualFeature.globalEmbedding,PhotoVisualFeature.patchGrid

function FindSimilarAndroidPhotosFunctionPromise action compare:
  label "查看 Android 相似照片 Function Promise"
  summary "Ranks accessible photos with separate DINOv2 whole-scene, 4x4 composition, capture-time, registered face and pet, and general-subject evidence, then adds a non-scoring explanation from local VLM-derived tags."
  depends AndroidMediaLocationFieldPromise,PhotoVisualFeatureFieldPromise,FaceObservationFieldPromise,PetObservationFieldPromise,GeneralSubjectObservationFieldPromise,PhotoAnnotationFieldPromise,SimilarPhotoResultFieldPromise
  trigger "User taps 查看相似照片 on a photo with current visual features."
  precondition FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.query_feature statement "The query photo has a valid current DINOv2 feature set and remains accessible." refs AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,PhotoVisualFeature.photoId,PhotoVisualFeature.pipelineVersion
  reads AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.displayName,AndroidMediaLocation.dateTakenMillis,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,PhotoVisualFeature.photoId,PhotoVisualFeature.globalEmbedding,PhotoVisualFeature.dimension,PhotoVisualFeature.patchGrid,PhotoVisualFeature.gridSize,PhotoVisualFeature.modelName,PhotoVisualFeature.pipelineVersion,FaceObservation.photoId,FaceObservation.embedding,PetObservation.photoId,PetObservation.embedding,GeneralSubjectObservation.photoId,GeneralSubjectObservation.category,GeneralSubjectObservation.embedding,PhotoAnnotation.photoId,PhotoAnnotation.tags,PhotoAnnotation.facets
  writes -
  ensure FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.global_similarity statement "Whole-scene similarity is cosine similarity between compatible normalized DINOv2 global vectors." refs SimilarPhotoResult.globalSimilarity,PhotoVisualFeature.globalEmbedding
  ensure FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.composition_similarity statement "Composition similarity compares corresponding row-major 4x4 cells and aggregates all sixteen bounded cell cosines without discarding spatial position." refs SimilarPhotoResult.compositionSimilarity,PhotoVisualFeature.patchGrid,PhotoVisualFeature.gridSize
  ensure FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.burst_evidence statement "Capture-time proximity can classify a high-global, high-composition pair as burst, but time alone cannot make visually dissimilar photos similar." refs AndroidMediaLocation.dateTakenMillis,SimilarPhotoResult.captureDeltaMillis,SimilarPhotoResult.relationship,SimilarPhotoResult.globalSimilarity,SimilarPhotoResult.compositionSimilarity
  ensure FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.subject_evidence statement "Subject similarity uses compatible maximum matching across existing face observations, existing same-species pet observations, and same-category general-subject observations; missing subject evidence remains null rather than zero." refs FaceObservation.embedding,PetObservation.embedding,GeneralSubjectObservation.category,GeneralSubjectObservation.embedding,SimilarPhotoResult.subjectSimilarity
  ensure FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.typed_relationship statement "Every candidate exposes independent global, composition, subject, and time evidence plus one primary relationship selected by deterministic versioned thresholds." refs SimilarPhotoResult.relationship,SimilarPhotoResult.globalSimilarity,SimilarPhotoResult.compositionSimilarity,SimilarPhotoResult.subjectSimilarity,SimilarPhotoResult.captureDeltaMillis,SimilarPhotoResult.rankScore
  ensure FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.accessible_only statement "The query and every candidate resolve to currently accessible MediaStore URIs and the same content identity is excluded." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,SimilarPhotoResult.queryPhotoId,SimilarPhotoResult.candidatePhotoId
  ensure FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.vlm_explanation_only statement "After ranking is final, overlapping local VLM-derived tags and facets may be rendered as why-similar text; removing or changing annotations cannot change scores, relationship, or ordering." refs PhotoAnnotation.tags,PhotoAnnotation.facets,SimilarPhotoResult.explanation,SimilarPhotoResult.rankScore
  reject FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.missing_feature statement "A photo without current valid visual features shows an indexing action and returns no fabricated similarity." refs PhotoVisualFeature.photoId,PhotoVisualFeature.pipelineVersion
  reject FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.incompatible_model statement "Features with different checkpoint identity, dimension, grid size, or pipeline version are not compared." refs PhotoVisualFeature.modelName,PhotoVisualFeature.dimension,PhotoVisualFeature.gridSize,PhotoVisualFeature.pipelineVersion
  sideeffect FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.read_only statement "Viewing similarity writes neither catalog state nor MediaStore and never deletes, moves, hides, or labels an original as redundant." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,SimilarPhotoResult.queryPhotoId,SimilarPhotoResult.candidatePhotoId
  idempotency "The same query against unchanged feature and accessibility state returns the same score-descending, content-id-stable order."
  forbid FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.no_vlm_ranking statement "VLM output and explanation text cannot contribute to candidate inclusion, numeric score, relationship class, or ordering." refs PhotoAnnotation.tags,PhotoAnnotation.facets,SimilarPhotoResult.rankScore,SimilarPhotoResult.relationship

function AnnotateAndroidPhotosFunctionPromise action annotate:
  label "Android VLM 标注 Function Promise"
  summary "Overlays anonymous markers on a bounded read-only thumbnail, sends it with an explicit context budget to the explicitly authorized Ollama endpoint for v6 grammar-safe semantics, validates marker-bound observations, and replaces markers with local person or pet names only on device."
  depends AndroidMediaLocationFieldPromise,AndroidAnnotationSelectionFieldPromise,InferenceConfigurationFieldPromise,PersonIdentityFieldPromise,FaceObservationFieldPromise,PetIdentityFieldPromise,PetObservationFieldPromise,PhotoAnnotationFieldPromise,AndroidSearchStateFieldPromise
  trigger "User invokes 标注所选 or 全量标注 for photos without this model and prompt version."
  precondition AnnotateAndroidPhotos.accessible statement "The content URI is currently accessible." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible
  precondition AnnotateAndroidPhotos.authorized_endpoint statement "The configured endpoint is loopback or allowRemote is true." refs InferenceConfiguration.endpoint,InferenceConfiguration.allowRemote
  reads AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,AndroidAnnotationSelection.photoIds,InferenceConfiguration.endpoint,InferenceConfiguration.modelName,InferenceConfiguration.allowRemote,FaceObservation.photoId,FaceObservation.faceIndex,FaceObservation.boundingBox,FaceObservation.matchState,FaceObservation.matchedIdentityId,PetObservation.photoId,PetObservation.petIndex,PetObservation.boundingBox,PetObservation.matchState,PetObservation.matchedIdentityId,PhotoAnnotation.promptVersion
  writes PhotoAnnotation.id,PhotoAnnotation.photoId,PhotoAnnotation.caption,PhotoAnnotation.tags,PhotoAnnotation.facets,PhotoAnnotation.visibleText,PhotoAnnotation.subjectMentions,PhotoAnnotation.recognizedSubjects,PhotoAnnotation.modelProvider,PhotoAnnotation.modelName,PhotoAnnotation.promptVersion,PhotoAnnotation.createdAt,AndroidSearchState.annotationCount,AndroidSearchState.enabled,AndroidSearchState.suggestions
  ensure AnnotateAndroidPhotos.structured_facets statement "Validated daylight, sky, counted objects, people presentation, actions, scenes, weather, tags, visible text, caption template, and anonymous subject mentions are committed atomically." refs PhotoAnnotation.caption,PhotoAnnotation.tags,PhotoAnnotation.facets,PhotoAnnotation.visibleText,PhotoAnnotation.subjectMentions
  ensure AnnotateAndroidPhotos.anonymous_overlay statement "The phone draws P1..Pn and PET1..PETn over local observation bounds on an in-memory copy; the prompt and schema contain only those markers and never contain identity labels, embeddings, or scores." refs FaceObservation.faceIndex,FaceObservation.boundingBox,PetObservation.petIndex,PetObservation.boundingBox,PhotoAnnotation.subjectMentions
  ensure AnnotateAndroidPhotos.bounded_thumbnail statement "The original is decoded only into an in-memory JPEG thumbnail whose longest edge is at most 1024 pixels for the first request; the original bytes are never encoded or uploaded." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri
  ensure AnnotateAndroidPhotos.context_budget statement "Every VLM annotation request asks Ollama for an 8192-token context window; if Ollama reports a request-context overflow, the app retries that photo at most once with a fresh thumbnail whose longest edge is at most 768 pixels." refs InferenceConfiguration.modelName,AndroidMediaLocation.uri
  ensure AnnotateAndroidPhotos.grammar_safe_schema statement "Every bounded free-text repetition in the JSON Schema sent to Ollama remains below the deployed llama.cpp grammar safety ceiling; newly generated visible text is limited to 512 characters while longer legacy annotations remain readable without migration." refs PhotoAnnotation.visibleText,InferenceConfiguration.modelName
  ensure AnnotateAndroidPhotos.local_name_substitution statement "At read time, validated markers are replaced locally with current accepted person or pet names; unknown markers render as numbered unknown labels and add no registered name to search." refs PhotoAnnotation.caption,PhotoAnnotation.subjectMentions,PhotoAnnotation.recognizedSubjects,FaceObservation.matchedIdentityId,PetObservation.matchedIdentityId
  ensure AnnotateAndroidPhotos.provenance statement "Provider, exact model, prompt version, and completion time are recorded." refs PhotoAnnotation.modelProvider,PhotoAnnotation.modelName,PhotoAnnotation.promptVersion,PhotoAnnotation.createdAt
  ensure AnnotateAndroidPhotos.enables_search statement "The first successful annotation enables search and suggestions are rebuilt from current annotation metadata." refs AndroidSearchState.annotationCount,AndroidSearchState.enabled,AndroidSearchState.suggestions
  ensure AnnotateAndroidPhotos.selected_scope_exact statement "标注所选 considers only currently accessible photo IDs in the latest explicit selection and cannot fall through to other catalog photos." refs AndroidAnnotationSelection.photoIds,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,PhotoAnnotation.photoId
  ensure AnnotateAndroidPhotos.full_scope_complete statement "全量标注 considers every currently accessible pending photo in one explicit run, including libraries larger than 20 photos; partial Android permission limits full scope to the user-authorized visible subset." refs AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,PhotoAnnotation.photoId
  ensure AnnotateAndroidPhotos.scope_visible statement "Progress and completion status identify 所选 or 全量 and report considered, succeeded, and failed counts." refs AndroidAnnotationSelection.photoIds,PhotoAnnotation.photoId
  reject AnnotateAndroidPhotos.no_selected_photos statement "标注所选 with no completed non-empty selection sends no photo and directs the user to 选择照片 first." refs AndroidAnnotationSelection.photoIds
  reject AnnotateAndroidPhotos.invalid_output statement "Malformed, missing, excessive, non-positive-count facet data, an unoffered marker, a marker-kind mismatch, or an identity-like VLM subject field commits nothing." refs PhotoAnnotation.facets,PhotoAnnotation.subjectMentions
  reject AnnotateAndroidPhotos.context_overflow statement "A context overflow after the one bounded retry commits no annotation and remains a visible per-photo failure." refs PhotoAnnotation.id,AndroidMediaLocation.photoId
  reject AnnotateAndroidPhotos.schema_initialization_failure statement "A structured-output schema or grammar initialization failure commits no annotation and remains a visible per-photo failure." refs PhotoAnnotation.id,InferenceConfiguration.modelName
  reject AnnotateAndroidPhotos.model_failure statement "Network, endpoint, or model errors commit no partial annotation." refs InferenceConfiguration.endpoint,InferenceConfiguration.modelName
  sideeffect AnnotateAndroidPhotos.explicit_transfer statement "Only after endpoint authorization, a resized in-memory image copy is sent to that endpoint; the original remains unchanged." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,InferenceConfiguration.endpoint,InferenceConfiguration.allowRemote
  idempotency "Within either scope, the same model and prompt version is skipped unless the user explicitly requests re-annotation; changing scope does not duplicate current annotations."
  forbid AnnotateAndroidPhotos.no_identity_guess statement "The VLM cannot receive or emit person or pet names or influence local matching; unknown subjects remain explicitly unknown, and no relationship, sensitive trait, or actual gender is inferred." refs PhotoAnnotation.facets,PhotoAnnotation.subjectMentions,PhotoAnnotation.recognizedSubjects,FaceObservation.matchedIdentityId,PetObservation.matchedIdentityId

function SearchAndroidGalleryFunctionPromise action search:
  label "搜索 Android 相册 Function Promise"
  summary "Matches descriptions, structured facets, tags, and visible text in app-private SQLite and displays only currently accessible MediaStore items."
  depends AndroidMediaLocationFieldPromise,PersonIdentityFieldPromise,FaceObservationFieldPromise,PetIdentityFieldPromise,PetObservationFieldPromise,PhotoAnnotationFieldPromise,AndroidSearchStateFieldPromise
  trigger "User enters text or selects a facet in the Android app."
  precondition SearchAndroidGallery.query statement "The normalized text query or selected facet is non-empty." refs PhotoAnnotation.caption,PhotoAnnotation.tags,PhotoAnnotation.facets,PhotoAnnotation.visibleText
  precondition SearchAndroidGallery.annotation_exists statement "At least one current photo annotation exists and search is enabled." refs AndroidSearchState.annotationCount,AndroidSearchState.enabled
  reads AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.photoId,AndroidMediaLocation.displayName,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible,PersonIdentity.id,PersonIdentity.name,FaceObservation.photoId,FaceObservation.matchState,FaceObservation.matchedIdentityId,PetIdentity.id,PetIdentity.name,PetObservation.photoId,PetObservation.matchState,PetObservation.matchedIdentityId,PhotoAnnotation.photoId,PhotoAnnotation.caption,PhotoAnnotation.tags,PhotoAnnotation.facets,PhotoAnnotation.visibleText,PhotoAnnotation.subjectMentions,PhotoAnnotation.id,AndroidSearchState.annotationCount,AndroidSearchState.enabled,AndroidSearchState.suggestions
  writes -
  ensure SearchAndroidGallery.latest statement "Results use the latest annotation per photo and include searchable provenance." refs PhotoAnnotation.id,PhotoAnnotation.photoId,PhotoAnnotation.modelName,PhotoAnnotation.promptVersion
  ensure SearchAndroidGallery.accessible_only statement "Results contain only accessible=true content URIs." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible
  ensure SearchAndroidGallery.annotation_derived_suggestions statement "Suggestion chips are empty before annotation and afterwards come only from latest accessible annotation metadata." refs AndroidSearchState.annotationCount,AndroidSearchState.suggestions
  ensure SearchAndroidGallery.local_identity_names statement "Matched PersonIdentity and PetIdentity names are searchable and displayed dynamically from current local observations, while unknown subjects add no registered name." refs PersonIdentity.name,FaceObservation.matchState,FaceObservation.matchedIdentityId,PetIdentity.name,PetObservation.matchState,PetObservation.matchedIdentityId,PhotoAnnotation.recognizedSubjects
  reject SearchAndroidGallery.empty statement "Whitespace-only search is rejected while the annotated gallery may list recent annotations." refs PhotoAnnotation.caption
  reject SearchAndroidGallery.no_annotations statement "Search input, submission, and suggestions remain disabled and empty before the first annotation." refs AndroidSearchState.annotationCount,AndroidSearchState.enabled,AndroidSearchState.suggestions
  sideeffect SearchAndroidGallery.read_only statement "Search writes neither the catalog nor MediaStore." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri
  idempotency "The same query against unchanged local state returns the same newest-first results."
  forbid SearchAndroidGallery.no_hidden_uri statement "Never display a result that is no longer permission-accessible." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible

function AgentSearchPhotosFunctionPromise action search:
  label "Agent 搜索照片 Function Promise"
  summary "Uses a minimal model planner and one local search skill to execute a bounded compound photo query."
  depends AndroidMediaLocationFieldPromise,InferenceConfigurationFieldPromise,PersonIdentityFieldPromise,FaceObservationFieldPromise,PetIdentityFieldPromise,PetObservationFieldPromise,PhotoAnnotationFieldPromise,AndroidSearchStateFieldPromise
  trigger "User submits a non-empty natural-language request on the Agent search screen."
  precondition AgentSearchPhotos.annotation_exists statement "At least one current annotation exists and local search is enabled." refs AndroidSearchState.annotationCount,AndroidSearchState.enabled
  precondition AgentSearchPhotos.authorized_endpoint statement "The configured planner endpoint is loopback or explicitly authorized." refs InferenceConfiguration.endpoint,InferenceConfiguration.allowRemote
  reads InferenceConfiguration.endpoint,InferenceConfiguration.modelName,InferenceConfiguration.allowRemote,PersonIdentity.name,FaceObservation.matchState,PetIdentity.name,PetObservation.matchState,PhotoAnnotation.caption,PhotoAnnotation.tags,PhotoAnnotation.facets,PhotoAnnotation.visibleText,PhotoAnnotation.recognizedSubjects,AndroidSearchState.enabled
  writes -
  ensure AgentSearchPhotos.bounded_plan statement "The planner returns one to four non-empty search queries through a strict JSON schema." refs PhotoAnnotation.caption,PhotoAnnotation.tags,PhotoAnnotation.facets,PhotoAnnotation.recognizedSubjects
  ensure AgentSearchPhotos.skill_invocation statement "Every planned query is executed through the single read-only local photo-search skill and results are deduplicated by photo identity." refs PhotoAnnotation.photoId
  ensure AgentSearchPhotos.accessible_only statement "Agent results inherit the local search guarantee and contain only currently accessible items." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,AndroidMediaLocation.accessible
  reject AgentSearchPhotos.empty_request statement "An empty natural-language request is rejected before planner invocation." refs PhotoAnnotation.caption
  reject AgentSearchPhotos.invalid_plan statement "Malformed, empty, or over-broad planner output is rejected without catalog changes." refs PhotoAnnotation.caption
  sideeffect AgentSearchPhotos.text_only_planning statement "Only the request text and locally registered person and pet labels are sent to the configured planner; embeddings, match scores, photo bytes, and indexed captions are not sent." refs PersonIdentity.name,PetIdentity.name,InferenceConfiguration.endpoint
  idempotency "The same plan against unchanged catalog state returns the same locally ordered, deduplicated results."
  forbid AgentSearchPhotos.no_mutation_tool statement "The Agent has no scan, annotation, delete, move, rename, or catalog-write tool." refs AndroidMediaLocation.uri,PhotoAnnotation.id

verify PhotoIdentityVerification kind field:
  label "照片身份验证"
  claim "Duplicate bytes at multiple paths share one PhotoAsset while retaining all current paths."
  verifies PhotoAssetFieldPromise,PhotoLocationFieldPromise
  methods unit,integration
  scenario "duplicate content at two paths":
    covers PhotoAsset.id_is_content_hash,ScanLibrary.content_addressed
    given "Two supported files contain identical bytes at different paths."
    when "The common root is scanned."
    then "One PhotoAsset and two present PhotoLocation records exist."
    guard "Neither source file is changed."
  evidence "Automated database assertions plus before-and-after source hashes."
  fail "Content identity changes without byte changes or one location is lost."

verify LocalAnnotationVerification kind function:
  label "本地标注验证"
  claim "Validated multimodal output is appended with exact provenance and becomes searchable."
  verifies TagPhotoFunctionPromise,PhotoAnnotationFieldPromise
  methods unit,integration
  scenario "successful local annotation":
    covers TagPhoto.validated_structured_output,TagPhoto.provenance_recorded,PhotoAnnotation.provenance_complete
    given "A present photo and a deterministic local model response matching the schema."
    when "Annotation runs for the configured model and prompt version."
    then "One immutable annotation exists and its caption, tags, visible text, model, and prompt version are indexed."
    guard "The original file hash is unchanged."
  scenario "invalid model output":
    covers TagPhoto.invalid_output
    given "The model response omits required structured fields."
    when "Annotation is attempted."
    then "No annotation or partial search record is written."
    guard "A later valid retry can succeed."
  evidence "Model adapter tests and transactional database assertions."
  fail "Invalid or unattributed metadata is committed."

verify SearchVerification kind function:
  label "照片搜索验证"
  claim "Chinese and Latin queries can match latest captions, tags, or visible text and return current local paths only."
  verifies SearchPhotosFunctionPromise
  methods unit,integration
  scenario "search generated tag":
    covers SearchPhotos.latest_annotation,SearchPhotos.current_paths_only
    given "A photo has a latest annotation containing the Chinese tag 海边 and a current local path."
    when "The user searches for 海边."
    then "The current path and annotation provenance are returned."
    guard "An absent path for the same photo is not returned."
  evidence "SQLite query tests covering Chinese substring and Latin token matching."
  fail "A matching present photo is omitted or an absent path is returned."

verify PrivacyBoundaryVerification kind cross-cutting:
  label "隐私边界验证"
  claim "The default inference endpoint is loopback and originals remain read-only."
  verifies ScanLibraryFunctionPromise,TagPhotoFunctionPromise
  methods unit,review
  scenario "default local-only workflow":
    covers ScanLibrary.no_source_write,TagPhoto.local_default,TagPhoto.no_implicit_remote
    given "No provider-related environment variables are configured."
    when "The user scans and annotates a photo."
    then "Only the local catalog changes and inference targets a loopback Ollama URL."
    guard "Non-loopback endpoints require an explicit user-provided URL."
  evidence "Default configuration assertions and source hash checks."
  fail "A default request can send bytes off-device or mutate a source file."

verify LocalFaceIdentityVerification kind cross-cutting:
  label "本地人物注册与匹配验证"
  claim "One explicitly selected reference face creates an app-private embedding template, later photos match only above strict confidence and ambiguity gates, and VLM output never decides person identity."
  verifies PersonIdentityFieldPromise,FaceTemplateFieldPromise,FaceObservationFieldPromise,RegisterPersonIdentityFunctionPromise,MatchAndroidFacesFunctionPromise
  methods unit,integration,review
  scenario "tap one reference face and register name":
    covers PersonIdentity.no_implicit_identity,FaceTemplate.selected_face_only,FaceTemplate.no_reference_pixels,RegisterPersonIdentity.selected_embedding,RegisterPersonIdentity.local_only,RegisterPersonIdentity.no_reference_retention
    given "The Photo Picker returns a readable image with two locally detected faces."
    when "The user taps only the first face, enters 小明, and saves."
    then "One 小明 identity and one normalized template for the tapped bounding box exist; no bitmap, crop, or image bytes are stored or uploaded."
    guard "The untapped face creates no identity or template."
  scenario "oversized frontal face survives detector scaling":
    covers FaceObservation.one_physical_face_once,RegisterPersonIdentity.scale_robust_reference,MatchAndroidFaces.multiscale_coverage,MatchAndroidFaces.cross_scale_dedup,MatchAndroidFaces.pipeline_reindex
    given "A clear frontal face fills most of a high-resolution reference photo and the same source can produce overlapping YuNet candidates at multiple bounded scales."
    when "The bundled local face pipeline detects, maps, deduplicates, aligns, and embeds the photo."
    then "Exactly one spatially ordered face observation represents that physical face, its original-space box remains large, and its finite normalized embedding is available for registration."
    guard "Existing compatible face templates remain usable, stale zero-face index rows do not suppress reprocessing, and no source pixels are modified or retained."
  scenario "same person clears threshold and ambiguity margin":
    covers FaceObservation.explicit_unknown,MatchAndroidFaces.threshold_and_margin,MatchAndroidFaces.current_provenance,SearchAndroidGallery.local_identity_names
    given "A scanned face has cosine similarity 0.82 to 小明 and 0.40 to every other identity with threshold 0.55 and margin 0.05."
    when "The bundled local matcher indexes the photo."
    then "The observation is matched to 小明 with model, score, threshold, bounds, and time, and an annotated accessible photo is searchable by 小明."
    guard "No VLM response or person candidate contributes to the score."
  scenario "low confidence and ambiguity stay unknown":
    covers FaceObservation.explicit_unknown,MatchAndroidFaces.unknown_by_default,MatchAndroidFaces.no_vlm_person_decision
    given "One face scores 0.54 for its best identity and another scores 0.72 versus 0.70 for two different identities."
    when "Both observations are matched."
    then "Both are stored as unknown with no matchedIdentityId and add no searchable person name."
    guard "Lowering a threshold or choosing the top name implicitly is forbidden."
  scenario "new registration rematches existing local embeddings":
    covers RegisterPersonIdentity.rematch_existing,MatchAndroidFaces.local_database_only
    given "An already scanned annotated photo contains an unknown stored face observation."
    when "The user registers a matching reference face under 小红."
    then "Stored observations are rematched locally and the existing photo becomes searchable by 小红 without rerunning the VLM."
    guard "No original or reference photo pixels are persisted or sent over the network."
  scenario "VLM cannot identify a person":
    covers RecognitionProfile.android_vlm_no_identity,FaceObservation.no_vlm_identity,AnnotateAndroidPhotos.no_identity_guess
    given "The VLM returns or attempts to return a person name or an unoffered subject marker."
    when "The v5 Android annotation contract validates the response."
    then "The identity output is rejected and only accepted local FaceObservation names appear in search."
    guard "Neither person nor pet candidate names are present in the VLM request."
  evidence "Promise gates, oversized-face multi-scale and cross-scale dedup regression tests, matcher and database migration tests, bundled-model checksum and license evidence, Android unit tests, debug build and lint, plus emulator acceptance without mutating a real phone."
  fail "A clear close-up face is missed only because it is large, one face becomes duplicate observations across scales, stale zero-face rows suppress the new pipeline, registration can occur without a tapped face, reference pixels leave app memory, a low or ambiguous score receives a name, the VLM determines a person identity, model provenance is missing, or a matched name is not searchable."

verify LocalPetIdentityVerification kind cross-cutting:
  label "本地宠物注册与匹配验证"
  claim "One explicitly selected detected cat or dog creates an app-private visual template, later same-species observations match only above conservative confidence and ambiguity gates, and VLM output never decides pet identity."
  verifies PetIdentityFieldPromise,PetTemplateFieldPromise,PetObservationFieldPromise,RegisterPetIdentityFunctionPromise,MatchAndroidPetsFunctionPromise
  methods unit,integration,review
  scenario "tap one detected pet and register name":
    covers PetIdentity.no_implicit_identity,PetTemplate.selected_pet_only,PetTemplate.no_reference_pixels,RegisterPetIdentity.selected_embedding,RegisterPetIdentity.local_only,RegisterPetIdentity.no_reference_retention
    given "The Photo Picker returns a readable image with two locally detected dogs."
    when "The user selects pet mode, taps only the first dog, enters 旺财, and saves."
    then "One 旺财 pet identity and one normalized dog template for the tapped bounding box exist; no bitmap, crop, or image bytes are stored or uploaded."
    guard "The untapped dog creates no identity or template."
  scenario "same pet clears conservative threshold":
    covers PetObservation.explicit_unknown,MatchAndroidPets.same_species_only,MatchAndroidPets.threshold_and_margin,SearchAndroidGallery.local_identity_names
    given "A dog observation scores 0.94 to 旺财 and 0.70 to every other dog identity with threshold 0.90 and margin 0.04."
    when "The bundled local matcher indexes the photo."
    then "The observation is matched to 旺财 with species, model, score, threshold, bounds, and time, and the annotated accessible photo is searchable by 旺财."
    guard "Cat templates and VLM output cannot contribute to the decision."
  scenario "low confidence and ambiguity stay unknown":
    covers PetObservation.explicit_unknown,MatchAndroidPets.unknown_by_default,MatchAndroidPets.no_vlm_pet_decision
    given "One pet scores 0.89 for its best same-species identity and another scores 0.95 versus 0.93 for two dog identities."
    when "Both observations are matched."
    then "Both are stored as unknown with no matchedIdentityId and add no searchable pet name."
    guard "The top candidate is never forced into a match."
  scenario "new pet registration rematches stored observations":
    covers RegisterPetIdentity.rematch_existing,MatchAndroidPets.local_database_only
    given "An already scanned annotated photo contains an unknown stored dog observation."
    when "The user registers a matching dog reference under 旺财."
    then "Stored dog observations are rematched locally and the existing photo becomes searchable by 旺财 without rerunning the VLM."
    guard "No original or reference pixels leave app memory."
  evidence "Promise gates, pet matcher and database migration tests, bundled detector and embedder checksums and license evidence, Android model-load integration tests, debug build and lint, plus emulator acceptance without mutating a real phone."
  fail "Pet registration occurs without an explicit tap, reference pixels are retained, species are crossed, a low or ambiguous score receives a name, the VLM decides pet identity, provenance is missing, or a matched pet name is not searchable."

verify AnonymousSubjectAnnotationVerification kind cross-cutting:
  label "匿名主体标注与本地替换验证"
  claim "VLM sees only numbered overlays, returns only allowed marker-bound semantics, and current person or pet names are substituted and searched only on the phone."
  verifies PhotoAnnotationFieldPromise,AnnotateAndroidPhotosFunctionPromise,SearchAndroidGalleryFunctionPromise
  methods unit,integration,review
  scenario "two people and one pet use anonymous markers":
    covers PhotoAnnotation.anonymous_markers_only,AnnotateAndroidPhotos.anonymous_overlay,AnnotateAndroidPhotos.local_name_substitution,PhotoAnnotation.recognized_subjects_constrained
    given "A photo has matched P1=小明, unknown P2, and matched PET1=旺财 local observations."
    when "The phone overlays P1, P2, and PET1 and the VLM returns a valid caption template plus marker-bound actions."
    then "The HTTP request contains no 小明 or 旺财, stored model output contains markers rather than names, and the UI renders 小明, 未知人物2, and 旺财 locally."
    guard "Only 小明 and 旺财 become searchable registered names; the unknown observation stays unnamed."
  scenario "unoffered marker or identity field is rejected":
    covers AnnotateAndroidPhotos.invalid_output,AnnotateAndroidPhotos.no_identity_guess
    given "Only P1 was overlaid but the model returns P2, a mismatched PET1 kind, or a real-name identity field."
    when "The response is validated."
    then "No annotation row is committed."
    guard "The original photo and local match rows remain unchanged."
  scenario "new template updates old annotation without VLM rerun":
    covers AnnotateAndroidPhotos.local_name_substitution,SearchAndroidGallery.local_identity_names
    given "An existing annotation template contains P1 and its current observation is unknown."
    when "The user later registers a matching local person template."
    then "The same stored annotation renders and searches the newly accepted name from current local rows without changing model output or rerunning VLM."
    guard "The historical model output remains immutable."
  evidence "Strict schema tests, request-capture tests proving name absence, local marker-substitution tests, database rematch tests, and emulator UI verification."
  fail "A real identity label reaches or comes from VLM, an unoffered marker is accepted, unknown is force-matched, replacement is persisted as model truth, or rematching requires a VLM rerun."

verify VisualSimilarityVerification kind cross-cutting:
  label "整图与主体视觉相似验证"
  claim "One 检查相似 entry explicitly selects incremental, custom recent, or full scope; the public on-device DINOv2 ViT-S/14 registers pipeline then refreshes only that scope, produces whole-photo and 4x4 spatial features, ranks burst, same-scene, composition, and subject relationships independently, and allows VLM-derived tags to explain but never decide similarity."
  verifies SimilarityCheckRequestFieldPromise,PhotoVisualFeatureFieldPromise,GeneralSubjectObservationFieldPromise,SimilarPhotoResultFieldPromise,CheckAndroidVisualSimilarityFunctionPromise,IndexAndroidVisualSimilarityFunctionPromise,FindSimilarAndroidPhotosFunctionPromise
  methods unit,integration,review
  scenario "one check button enforces three explicit scopes":
    covers SimilarityCheckRequest.explicit_mode,SimilarityCheckRequest.recent_complete,SimilarityCheckRequest.no_hidden_recent_fallback,CheckAndroidVisualSimilarity.one_button_three_modes,CheckAndroidVisualSimilarity.refresh_visibility,CheckAndroidVisualSimilarity.incremental_scope,CheckAndroidVisualSimilarity.recent_scope,CheckAndroidVisualSimilarity.full_scope,CheckAndroidVisualSimilarity.scope_report,CheckAndroidVisualSimilarity.invalid_recent,CheckAndroidVisualSimilarity.no_predelete
    given "The catalog contains one current-feature photo, one newly visible unindexed photo, one old unindexed photo, one recently captured current-feature photo, and one accessible photo without capture time."
    when "The user separately confirms incremental, a custom recent duration, and full checks from 检查相似."
    then "Incremental selects only missing current features, recent recomputes only real capture times inside the exact cutoff and reports the unknown-time exclusion, and full recomputes every accessible photo with visible considered, success, and failure counts."
    guard "Invalid recent input starts no work, partial access reopens reselection, and a failed forced replacement leaves its older feature readable."
  scenario "real DINOv2 photo produces global and spatial features":
    covers PhotoVisualFeature.normalized_global,PhotoVisualFeature.four_by_four_grid,PhotoVisualFeature.no_pixels,IndexAndroidVisualSimilarity.dinov2_global,IndexAndroidVisualSimilarity.four_by_four_patches,IndexAndroidVisualSimilarity.provenance,IndexAndroidVisualSimilarity.local_database_only
    given "A permission-accessible real photo and the checksum-verified public DINOv2 ViT-S/14 registers checkpoint are present on the Android device."
    when "The current visual pipeline indexes the photo from an orientation-corrected bounded thumbnail."
    then "One normalized global vector and exactly sixteen normalized row-major spatial cells with exact checkpoint and pipeline provenance are stored, and no bitmap, crop, or original copy remains."
    guard "Source MediaStore bytes and metadata remain unchanged and no network request occurs."
  scenario "capture time distinguishes a burst group":
    covers FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.global_similarity,FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.composition_similarity,FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.burst_evidence,FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.typed_relationship
    given "Three photos taken within two seconds have high whole-scene and aligned-grid similarity, while a fourth timestamp-adjacent photo is visually unrelated."
    when "The first photo opens 查看相似照片."
    then "The two visually matching photos are classified and grouped as burst with visible capture deltas; the unrelated photo is not promoted by time alone."
    guard "Changing only timestamps cannot make low-visual-similarity photos rank as burst."
  scenario "same subjects with different layout separates composition":
    covers FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.composition_similarity,FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.subject_evidence,FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.typed_relationship
    given "Two photos contain the same locally observed person and pet but place them in different 4x4 regions, while a third preserves the query layout."
    when "Similarity evidence is calculated."
    then "All may have subject evidence, but only the spatially aligned photo receives high composition similarity and the composition-similar relationship."
    guard "A high subject score cannot overwrite a low composition score."
  scenario "general object crop contributes subject evidence":
    covers GeneralSubjectObservation.valid_embedding,GeneralSubjectObservation.no_person_or_pet_duplication,IndexAndroidVisualSimilarity.general_subject_crops,IndexAndroidVisualSimilarity.reuse_identity_observations,FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.subject_evidence
    given "Two accessible photos contain a detector-supported bicycle, existing person and dog observations, and other low-quality boxes."
    when "The current pipeline indexes and compares them."
    then "The bicycle crops contribute same-category DINOv2 subject evidence, face and dog evidence comes from existing observation tables, and low-quality or person/cat/dog general detections are not duplicated."
    guard "No crop bitmap is retained or transmitted."
  scenario "VLM tags explain but cannot rank":
    covers SimilarPhotoResult.explanation_after_rank,SimilarPhotoResult.no_vlm_score,FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.vlm_explanation_only,FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.no_vlm_ranking
    given "An unchanged visual feature set is compared before and after its local annotations are replaced with different valid tags and facets."
    when "Similarity is requested in both states."
    then "Candidate inclusion, numeric scores, relationship classes, and ordering are identical; only the human-readable overlap explanation may change."
    guard "No caption, tag, facet, or VLM confidence enters any scoring function."
  scenario "inaccessible and incompatible features are excluded":
    covers FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.accessible_only,FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.incompatible_model,FindSimilarAndroidPhotos.missing_feature
    given "One candidate lost MediaStore permission, one uses a stale model pipeline, and one has no visual feature."
    when "The user opens current similarity results."
    then "None is fabricated or compared; the UI offers indexing where appropriate and shows only current compatible accessible candidates."
    guard "The read-only query does not mutate or delete stale derived rows."
  evidence "Promise gates, explicit scope and duration unit tests, SQLite incremental, recent, and full candidate tests, deterministic scoring and classification tests, real DINOv2 model-output integration tests, source-hash preservation, isolated debug build and lint, plus emulator and data-preserving real-device UI acceptance."
  fail "The check button omits a mode, recent input silently defaults or broadens scope, incremental recomputes current photos, recent includes missing capture times, full hides a count cap, a failed refresh pre-deletes a valid feature, a fake or non-DINO vector is accepted as current, the grid is missing or unordered, VLM metadata changes ranking, inaccessible photos appear, provenance is absent, crops are retained, or originals are mutated."

verify PhotoViewerVerification kind cross-cutting:
  label "APM 应用内照片查看验证"
  claim "Every APM photo-result surface opens the exact accessible photo in a private native viewer at its complete original image resolution, with original-pixel zoom, read-only adjacent navigation, and bounded pan, without relying on an external image app."
  verifies AndroidPhotoViewerFieldPromise,ViewAndroidPhotoFunctionPromise
  methods unit,integration,review
  scenario "all photo surfaces open the exact item inside APM":
    covers AndroidPhotoViewer.accessible_sequence,AndroidPhotoViewer.no_external_handoff,ViewAndroidPhoto.in_app_destination,ViewAndroidPhoto.exact_initial_selection,ViewAndroidPhoto.no_external_view
    given "The accessible wall contains photos A, B, and C, while B appears in the wall, text search, Agent search, and similar-photo results."
    when "The user taps B from each surface."
    then "Each route starts private PhotoViewerActivity at B with position 2 of 3 and no external chooser or image application appears."
    guard "No entry point constructs or dispatches ACTION_VIEW for B's content URI."
  scenario "original resolution and gestures stay truthful":
    covers AndroidPhotoViewer.original_decode,AndroidPhotoViewer.zoom_bounds,ViewAndroidPhoto.aspect_fit,ViewAndroidPhoto.zoom_and_pan
    given "A readable 3072 by 2048 original whose longest edge exceeds the former 2048 thumbnail bound."
    when "It opens, is pinched to native-pixel scale, panned, reset, and then the next photo is selected."
    then "The in-memory bitmap is exactly 3072 by 2048, the complete aspect-preserving original starts fit at scale 1, the maximum scale reaches at least one original pixel per display pixel and at least 5, pan stays bounded, and the next photo starts at scale 1 with zero pan."
    guard "No loadThumbnail call, target-size request, sampled decode, crop, persisted derivative, or source-byte mutation is allowed."
  scenario "navigation and read failure remain inside the viewer":
    covers ViewAndroidPhoto.adjacent_navigation,ViewAndroidPhoto.inaccessible_or_unreadable,ViewAndroidPhoto.read_only,AndroidPhotoViewer.no_original_mutation
    given "Three ordered accessible photos where the middle URI becomes unreadable after the viewer opens."
    when "The user navigates from the first to the middle and then to the last photo."
    then "Boundary controls and one-based position are exact, the middle page shows an in-app read error, and navigation to the last remains possible."
    guard "No original, MediaStore row, annotation row, or external application is modified or opened."
  evidence "Promise gates, pure JVM viewer navigation and native-pixel zoom-bound tests, source inspection proving every photo-card route targets PhotoViewerActivity and no viewer loadThumbnail remains, an API 35 assertion that a 3072 by 2048 MediaStore original decodes to exactly 3072 by 2048 with unchanged SHA-256, isolated Android build and lint, and emulator interaction covering open, fit, zoom, pan, reset, adjacent navigation, back, and empty AndroidRuntime errors."
  fail "Any photo tap leaves APM, selects the wrong photo, omits an in-app read failure, downsamples, samples, targets a smaller size, or crops the original decode, stretches the image, prevents native-pixel inspection, permits unbounded pan, loses adjacent navigation, mutates an original, or crashes during interaction."

verify PhotoWallVerification kind cross-cutting:
  label "Android 按日照片墙验证"
  claim "The native gallery separates its photo wall and heatmap into dedicated pages, presents every distinct currently accessible photo under its real device-local capture day, and exposes one-screen vertically chronological GitHub-style annual daily, weekly, and monthly heatmaps with vertical side controls and exact range filtering."
  verifies AndroidPhotoWallFieldPromise,BrowseAndroidPhotoWallFunctionPromise
  methods unit,integration,review
  scenario "all accessible photos appear without an annotation or search cap":
    covers AndroidPhotoWall.accessible_distinct,AndroidPhotoWall.no_annotation_gate,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.all_accessible_photos,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.inaccessible
    given "The catalog contains more than one hundred distinct accessible photos, including unannotated photos and duplicate accessible locations, plus one inaccessible annotated photo."
    when "The gallery photo-wall projection is loaded."
    then "Every accessible photoId appears exactly once, an accessible URI is selected, unannotated photos remain visible, and the inaccessible photo is absent."
    guard "The projection does not reuse the bounded annotation search query."
  scenario "capture day is real and unknown time stays unknown":
    covers AndroidPhotoWall.real_capture_day,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.day_sections,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.no_date_fallback
    given "Photos straddle a midnight boundary in the device time zone and another photo has null dateTakenMillis but newer modified and annotation times."
    when "Day groups are organized."
    then "Each dated photo belongs to its device-local capture day in newest-first order and the null-timestamp photo appears only in the final unknown-time group."
    guard "No modified, discovery, index, or annotation time is consulted as a fallback."
  scenario "thumbnail and detail modes preserve the same wall":
    covers AndroidPhotoWall.mode_preserves_membership,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.thumbnail_mode,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.detail_mode
    given "The wall contains dated and unknown-time photos with a mix of annotated and unannotated rows."
    when "The user switches between thumbnail and detail presentation."
    then "The photoId sequence, group membership, selected range, displayed year, heatmap granularity, and daily counts are identical; only layout and optional detail content change."
    guard "An unannotated detail card reports status without inventing a caption."
  scenario "photo wall and heatmap pages have exclusive content ownership":
    covers AndroidPhotoWall.page_ownership,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.dedicated_pages,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.range_filter
    given "The catalog contains dated photos and the gallery initially opens the dedicated photo-wall page."
    when "The user switches to heatmap, selects a populated range, and invokes the action to view those photos."
    then "The photo-wall page initially contains photo controls and cards with no heatmap, the independent heatmap page fuses vertical side controls with a borderless full-area one-screen vertically chronological annual grid with no photo cards, and the action returns to the photo-wall page with the exact range filter preserved."
    guard "No screen composition simultaneously exposes the annual heatmap and photo cards as one continuous content surface."
  scenario "right swipe opens the independent annual heatmap page":
    covers AndroidPhotoWall.page_ownership,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.dedicated_pages
    given "The photo wall is visible with at least one accessible photo and the annual heatmap action is available."
    when "The user swipes from left to right across the photo-wall surface."
    then "APM opens PhotoHeatmapActivity as a separate page, the heatmap page contains no photo cards, and its back action returns to the photo wall."
    guard "A short leftward or vertical photo-wall gesture does not open the heatmap page."
  scenario "bottom Dock owns global destinations":
    covers AndroidPhotoWall.page_ownership,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.dedicated_pages
    given "The main photo-wall page is visible."
    when "The user inspects the bottom Dock."
    then "The Dock exposes heatmap, people, Agent search, and settings in that order with settings at the far right, while the top app bar and photo-wall body do not duplicate those four destinations."
    guard "Each Dock action keeps its existing destination and does not mutate the photo catalog."
  scenario "story introduction is startup-only":
    covers AndroidPhotoWall.page_ownership
    given "The main activity is launched."
    when "The startup composition is shown and the user dismisses the introduction."
    then "The compact startup prompt says 让照片，自己说出故事, the large permanent hero block is absent from the photo-wall home, and the rest of the home remains available below the bottom Dock."
    guard "Returning from a child page does not reinsert the large story block into the home content."
  scenario "GitHub-style annual daily heatmap includes every date":
    covers AndroidPhotoWall.heatmap_exact_counts,AndroidPhotoWall.selected_range_exact,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.annual_heatmaps,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.range_filter
    given "A displayed year contains capture days with zero, one, two, and four distinct photos across several months."
    when "The user selects day granularity from the vertical side controls, sees the complete annual grid without scrolling, taps the two-photo date, moves to photos, and clears the selection."
    then "Every date in the year appears once in compact Sunday-through-Saturday rows, with each week below the previous week in chronological order; GitHub green levels are monotonic from zero through four, complete accessible date and count descriptions are present, and the selected two-photo range transfers exactly to the photo-wall page."
    guard "Padding dates outside the displayed year and zero-count dates cannot create a selected range."
  scenario "annual weekly aggregation is exact":
    covers AndroidPhotoWall.heatmap_exact_counts,AndroidPhotoWall.selected_range_exact,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.annual_heatmaps,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.range_filter
    given "Photos span a year boundary and several Sunday-through-Saturday weeks inside the displayed year."
    when "The user selects week granularity and taps a populated partial or full calendar week."
    then "The one-screen view contains every 53 or 54 intersecting week as compact chronological vertical rows, clips boundary ranges to the displayed year, reports each exact sum and accessible range, and filters only the selected week range."
    guard "No photo outside the displayed year or selected inclusive week range contributes to its count or filtered wall."
  scenario "annual monthly aggregation is exact":
    covers AndroidPhotoWall.heatmap_exact_counts,AndroidPhotoWall.selected_range_exact,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.annual_heatmaps,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.range_filter
    given "Photos occur in January, August, and December with other months empty."
    when "The user selects month granularity and taps populated August."
    then "All twelve months appear once as compact chronological vertical rows, each cell reports the exact monthly sum and mode-relative heat level, and only August capture-day groups remain after moving to the photo-wall page until cleared."
    guard "Empty months cannot create a selected range and changing year or granularity clears the prior range."
  evidence "Promise gates, pure JVM day-group, annual calendar, exact daily, weekly, and monthly aggregation and discrete-level tests, SQLite integration covering more than one hundred accessible annotated and unannotated photos, isolated Android build and lint, and API 35 emulator visual, semantics, startup-only story prompt, compact-home, bottom-Dock ownership/order, right-swipe navigation, page-isolation, one-screen/no-scroll, borderless full-area composition, vertical-order, side-control, granularity-switch, year-navigation, selection-transfer, and clear acceptance for all three GitHub-style heatmaps."
  fail "The wall hides an accessible unannotated photo, permanently reserves a large story hero block, omits or misorders a bottom-Dock destination, puts settings anywhere except the far right, omits or duplicates a bottom-Dock destination, fails the right-swipe route, places the heatmap inside the photo-wall page, displays photo cards inside the heatmap page, wraps the grid in a standalone frame, leaves the heatmap confined to a small inset instead of the available area, requires scrolling to see an annual grid or side control, lays a heatmap chronology horizontally, changes order between modes, omits a calendar date, week, or month, reports an inexact aggregate, leaks a boundary date into another year, assigns a non-monotonic or continuous-only heat level, diverges from the GitHub square green grid and 少-to-多 guide, omits an accessible range count, filters an empty cell, loses selection when moving to the photo-wall page, includes inaccessible photos, mutates an original, or fails lazy emulator rendering."

verify AndroidNativeAppVerification kind cross-cutting:
  label "Android Native App 验证"
  claim "A buildable native Android app completes permission-scoped scan, day-grouped browsing, private in-app photo viewing, DINOv2 visual similarity, local registered identity matching, anonymous structured VLM annotation, and local search without modifying MediaStore."
  verifies AndroidMediaLocationFieldPromise,AndroidPhotoWallFieldPromise,AndroidPhotoViewerFieldPromise,AndroidAnnotationSelectionFieldPromise,InferenceConfigurationFieldPromise,PersonIdentityFieldPromise,FaceTemplateFieldPromise,FaceObservationFieldPromise,PetIdentityFieldPromise,PetTemplateFieldPromise,PetObservationFieldPromise,SimilarityCheckRequestFieldPromise,PhotoVisualFeatureFieldPromise,GeneralSubjectObservationFieldPromise,SimilarPhotoResultFieldPromise,AndroidSearchStateFieldPromise,ConfigureAndroidModelFunctionPromise,RegisterPersonIdentityFunctionPromise,MatchAndroidFacesFunctionPromise,RegisterPetIdentityFunctionPromise,MatchAndroidPetsFunctionPromise,CheckAndroidVisualSimilarityFunctionPromise,IndexAndroidVisualSimilarityFunctionPromise,FindSimilarAndroidPhotosFunctionPromise,ScanAndroidGalleryFunctionPromise,BrowseAndroidPhotoWallFunctionPromise,ViewAndroidPhotoFunctionPromise,SelectAndroidPhotosForAnnotationFunctionPromise,AnnotateAndroidPhotosFunctionPromise,SearchAndroidGalleryFunctionPromise,AgentSearchPhotosFunctionPromise
  methods unit,integration,review
  scenario "scan annotate and search two dogs at night":
    covers ScanAndroidGallery.content_hash,AnnotateAndroidPhotos.structured_facets,SearchAndroidGallery.accessible_only
    given "A permission-visible photo and a deterministic VLM response describing two dogs outdoors at night."
    when "The user scans, annotates, and searches 天黑 or 狗."
    then "The result shows the current content URI, caption, 天黑, object 狗 count 2, scene, and exact model provenance."
    guard "The source MediaStore bytes and metadata are unchanged."
  scenario "remote endpoint without consent":
    covers ConfigureAndroidModel.remote_without_consent,AnnotateAndroidPhotos.authorized_endpoint
    given "The user enters a private-LAN or internet endpoint while remote permission is false."
    when "Settings are saved or annotation is requested."
    then "The operation is rejected before any photo bytes are read for upload."
    guard "Loopback remains the default configuration."
  scenario "invalid object count":
    covers AnnotateAndroidPhotos.invalid_output
    given "The model returns an object with count zero or omits a required facet."
    when "The response is parsed."
    then "No annotation or search document is committed."
    guard "A later valid retry remains possible."
  scenario "large source photo stays within bounded inference policy":
    covers AnnotateAndroidPhotos.bounded_thumbnail,AnnotateAndroidPhotos.context_budget,AnnotateAndroidPhotos.grammar_safe_schema,AnnotateAndroidPhotos.context_overflow,AnnotateAndroidPhotos.schema_initialization_failure,AnnotateAndroidPhotos.explicit_transfer
    given "A permission-visible high-resolution source photo whose 1600-pixel request would exceed a 4096-token Ollama context."
    when "The user annotates it through the configured local-network VLM."
    then "The first request contains only a JPEG thumbnail at most 1024 pixels on its longest edge, requests 8192 context tokens, and uses only grammar-safe bounded strings including at most 512 visible-text characters; a reported context overflow triggers at most one 768-pixel retry, and only a valid response is committed."
    guard "The original MediaStore bytes and metadata remain unchanged, and no request contains the original-resolution image."
  scenario "partial access can be reselected on every scan":
    covers ScanAndroidGallery.partial_reselection
    given "Android 14 or later grants selected-photo access but not full image access."
    when "The user invokes scan repeatedly."
    then "Each invocation launches the system reselection flow before scanning so newly selected photos can become visible."
    guard "Full-library access scans directly without a redundant permission prompt."
  scenario "selected annotation uses exact latest picker scope":
    covers AndroidAnnotationSelection.explicit_picker_only,AndroidAnnotationSelection.replace_not_union,SelectAndroidPhotosForAnnotation.exact_scope,SelectAndroidPhotosForAnnotation.preserve_other_access,AnnotateAndroidPhotos.selected_scope_exact,AnnotateAndroidPhotos.no_selected_photos
    given "The catalog has accessible photos A, B, and C; the user completes 选择照片 with A and C after a prior selection of B."
    when "The user invokes 标注所选."
    then "The current selection is exactly A and C, only pending A and C are considered, B remains catalog-accessible but is not sent, and the UI reports 所选 counts."
    guard "Cancelling 选择照片 or invoking 标注所选 with no selection sends no photo and never falls back to all accessible photos."
  scenario "full annotation covers all authorized pending photos":
    covers AnnotateAndroidPhotos.full_scope_complete,AnnotateAndroidPhotos.scope_visible,ScanAndroidGallery.permission_scoped_visibility
    given "Twenty-five photos are currently permission-accessible and pending for the configured model and prompt version."
    when "The user invokes 全量标注 and keeps the current permission choice."
    then "All twenty-five pending photos are considered once in that run, with progress and success or failure counts; no hidden twenty-photo cap remains."
    guard "With partial Android access, inaccessible library photos are neither queried nor sent."
  scenario "search starts empty and becomes annotation-derived":
    covers AndroidSearchState.enabled_after_annotation,AndroidSearchState.no_default_suggestions,AnnotateAndroidPhotos.enables_search,SearchAndroidGallery.annotation_derived_suggestions,SearchAndroidGallery.no_annotations
    given "The catalog has photos but no annotation."
    when "The main screen opens and then the first annotation succeeds."
    then "Initially search is disabled with no suggestion chips; afterwards it is enabled and chips are derived only from stored annotation facets and tags."
    guard "No hard-coded example search term appears before annotation."
  scenario "photo wall is independent from search and annotation state":
    covers BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.all_accessible_photos,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.day_sections,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.thumbnail_mode,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.detail_mode,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.dedicated_pages,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.annual_heatmaps,BrowseAndroidPhotoWall.range_filter
    given "The permission-visible catalog contains dated and unknown-time photos with mixed annotation state."
    when "The user browses days, switches thumbnail and detail modes, changes annual heatmap granularity, and selects a populated daily, weekly, or monthly range before running any text search."
    then "The wall remains complete and correctly grouped, the two display modes preserve order, all three annual heatmaps show exact counts, and the selected range filters only by real capture day."
    guard "Search limits, annotation presence, and non-capture timestamps cannot decide wall membership or grouping."
  scenario "photo taps stay inside APM":
    covers ViewAndroidPhoto.in_app_destination,ViewAndroidPhoto.exact_initial_selection,ViewAndroidPhoto.aspect_fit,ViewAndroidPhoto.adjacent_navigation
    given "An accessible photo appears in the wall and a search result."
    when "The user opens it from either surface, zooms it, and selects an adjacent photo."
    then "The private APM viewer shows the exact tapped photo fit without distortion, supports bounded inspection and correct adjacent navigation, and remains inside the app."
    guard "The URI is never handed to an external ACTION_VIEW application and the original stays read-only."
  scenario "dedicated Material 3 settings screen":
    covers ConfigureAndroidModel.dedicated_screen,ConfigureAndroidModel.local_identity_route
    given "The user opens model settings from the main Material 3 app bar."
    when "The settings destination is displayed and a valid configuration is saved."
    then "A separate screen shows endpoint, model, consent, a route to local person-and-pet registration, privacy explanation, back navigation, and save feedback before returning."
    guard "The gallery screen does not show a model settings dialog."
  scenario "person and pet identity stay local":
    covers RecognitionProfile.android_vlm_no_identity,AnnotateAndroidPhotos.anonymous_overlay,AnnotateAndroidPhotos.local_name_substitution,PhotoAnnotation.recognized_subjects_constrained,MatchAndroidFaces.threshold_and_margin,MatchAndroidPets.threshold_and_margin
    given "The user locally registers person 小明 and dog 旺财."
    when "A photo is locally matched, anonymously overlaid, and annotated by the VLM."
    then "小明 and 旺财 can appear only from accepted local observations, while the VLM sees and returns only Pn and PETn markers."
    guard "A name without an accepted same-kind local observation is omitted from recognized subjects."
  scenario "minimal Agent invokes only search skill":
    covers AgentSearchPhotos.bounded_plan,AgentSearchPhotos.skill_invocation,AgentSearchPhotos.accessible_only,AgentSearchPhotos.no_mutation_tool
    given "Search is enabled and accessible annotations include night, dog, and known-subject metadata."
    when "The user asks the Agent to find night photos containing 旺财."
    then "The planner emits one to four local queries, the search skill executes them, and deduplicated accessible results are displayed with the plan."
    guard "The Agent cannot modify the catalog or send photo bytes while planning."
  evidence "Promise gates, Python and JVM policy tests, photo-wall and photo-viewer navigation and bounds tests, over-one-hundred-photo SQLite wall projection tests, request-capture assertions for thumbnail dimensions and num_ctx, annotation-selection database migration and exact-scope tests, an over-twenty-photo full-scope test, Android debug build, zero-issue lint, bundled local identity-model verification, validated repository Agent skill, Compose semantics assertions, API 35 emulator photo-wall and in-app viewer interaction acceptance, and real Mac mini VLM inference."
  fail "The app cannot build, hides accessible photos behind annotation or search limits, misgroups a missing capture time, opens a photo outside APM, selects the wrong viewer item, downsamples or crops the original viewer image, prevents native-pixel inspection, mutates originals, uploads without consent, sends original-resolution inference bytes, retries context overflow more than once, annotates outside the latest explicit selection, silently broadens scope, accepts invalid facets or identity sources, gives the Agent mutation tools, names low-confidence identities, lets the VLM decide identity, returns inaccessible photos, keeps static search presets, enables search before annotation, fails partial reselection, uses a settings dialog, or materially diverges from Material Design 3 components and hierarchy."
